+## 16. Testing alternative histories
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-002-092 | How can an alleged pre-Columbian contact claim be evaluated without dismissing or accepting it by reputation? | Require dated context, materials and independent replication; distinguish contact from settlement. |
+| BANK-002-093 | What evidence would distinguish an ancient construction method from a modern reconstruction trick? | Compare period tools, material traces, scale and explicit assumptions. |
+| BANK-002-094 | Why does an alignment with a star require more than drawing a line on a map? | Inspect date, horizon, measurement uncertainty and multiple-comparison effects. |
+| BANK-002-095 | How can historical population estimates disagree without one researcher fabricating figures? | Compare definitions, source survival, models and uncertainty ranges. |
+| BANK-002-096 | What should a documentary do when its favorite explanation predicts evidence that has not been found? | State search coverage and competing predictions; avoid protecting the theory through unfalsifiable additions. |
