+# 003 Ancient India / Civilization: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**28 categories · 152 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Ancient India / Civilization. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Sources and chronological foundations
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-003-013 | How do inscriptions, coins and literature answer different questions about ancient India? | Compare dating, audience, geographic reach and survival bias; avoid treating one source class as universally superior. |
+| BANK-003-014 | Why do archaeological cultures and named kingdoms not map neatly onto each other? | Distinguish material classifications, political labels, linguistic evidence and retrospective historical categories. |
+| BANK-003-015 | How does an ancient Indian chronology combine relative and absolute dates? | Trace stratigraphy, inscriptions, astronomical claims and calibrated measurements within one bounded period. |
+| BANK-003-016 | What does decipherment of Brahmi allow historians to investigate? | Explain the history of the decipherment and a sourced inscription example; distinguish reading characters from resolving interpretation. |
+| BANK-003-017 | How can a royal inscription exaggerate power while preserving useful evidence? | Analyze titles, patronage, genre and independent geographic or material corroboration. |
+
