+# 004 Sanatan / Hindu Mythology: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**25 categories · 144 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Sanatan / Hindu Mythology. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Reading sacred narratives
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-004-017 | Why can two Hindu texts tell different versions of the same divine event? | Compare genre, source date, sectarian perspective and narrative purpose rather than treating variation as a copying error. |
+| BANK-004-018 | How do a Purana, an epic and a temple mahatmya make different kinds of claims? | Use identified passages and explain audience, textual context and the limits of historical inference. |
+| BANK-004-019 | What is lost when dharma is translated only as duty? | Compare a small set of attributed passages and translations; preserve contextual meanings instead of supplying one universal equivalent. |
+| BANK-004-020 | How should a video distinguish scripture, commentary, folklore and modern invention? | Build a visible source trail for one story and label additions rather than silently blending authority levels. |
+| BANK-004-021 | Why must a quotation's wording be checked against its actual source? | Compare a circulated saying with traceable Sanskrit or vernacular editions; separate translation, paraphrase and misattribution. |
+
+## 02. Creation and sacred time
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
