+| BANK-004-143 | How does Trijata's dream function inside the narrative rather than as a general dream-prediction manual? | Locate the episode, speaker and audience in the chosen edition; compare the reassurance it offers with later interpretations without endorsing divination claims. |
+| BANK-004-144 | What does Mandodari's lament ask an audience to reconsider about Ravana? | Use actual speeches and their setting in a named text; preserve grief and moral complexity without rewriting the antagonist's actions or imposing one modern judgment. |
+| BANK-004-145 | How can an Uttara Kanda retelling disclose edition and reception debates respectfully? | Identify the chosen text's inclusion, scholarly apparatus and distinct devotional reception; separate textual-critical questions from a verdict on a community's faith. |
+
+## 23. Mahabharata dialogues, witnesses and aftermath
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-004-146 | How does the Sulabha-Janaka dialogue examine identity and authority? | Read the complete bounded dialogue in a specified translation and commentary; keep philosophical terms contextual and avoid reducing the exchange to a modern slogan. |
+| BANK-004-147 | What choices does Kunti describe when Karna learns about his birth? | Follow the encounter's timing, requests and responses in one edition; label later dramatizations and preserve the distinction between narrated knowledge and audience knowledge. |
+| BANK-004-148 | How does Gandhari's grief shape the Mahabharata's account of victory? | Trace selected postwar passages and their speakers; avoid editing a lament into an uncomplicated endorsement of any side. |
+| BANK-004-149 | What does the mongoose episode question about the meaning of giving? | Read the episode within its narrative setting and compare one attributed interpretation; distinguish its ethical contrast from a prescription for household donations. |
+| BANK-004-150 | How do accounts of Abhimanyu's death distribute knowledge and responsibility among characters? | Use a specified edition to track who knows the formation, actions and reported events; exclude unsupported claims about prenatal learning as established science. |
+
+## 24. Regional-language devotional canons
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-004-151 | How does an Andal hymn address the divine differently from a prose biography of Andal? | Identify one hymn, its Tamil text, translation and authorized public commentary; separate the poem's voice from later hagiographic episodes. |
+| BANK-004-152 | What does a selected Nammalvar verse reveal when read with its traditional commentary? | Bound the episode to one verse and named commentary, explaining key Tamil terms; avoid claiming that one English rendering contains every theological meaning. |
+| BANK-004-153 | How do Appar and Sambandar describe the same sacred place in selected Tevaram hymns? | Verify hymn attribution, place and translation for both selections; preserve distinct poetic situations rather than presenting all Shaiva hymns as interchangeable. |
+| BANK-004-154 | How can a Tukaram abhang be interpreted when modern song performances alter its wording? | Compare a traceable Marathi text, attributed translation and the actual performance transcript; verify adaptation rights and do not treat a popular recording as the textual edition. |
+| BANK-004-155 | What should a Kabir episode disclose about competing collections and attributions? | Identify the exact collection and verse witnesses, compare an attributed translation and preserve uncertainty; avoid assigning every circulating couplet to Kabir. |
+
+## 25. Festivals, narrative variants and iconographic attributes
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-004-156 | How do public accounts of Onam frame Mahabali's return in different Kerala communities? | Use authorized community accounts and source-specific narrative references; distinguish contemporary festival meaning from proof of a single historical origin. |
+| BANK-004-157 | How do Vishu and a New Year festival elsewhere differ in calendar logic and public symbolism? | Check the particular region, year and official or community calendar before comparison; do not assume every Hindu New Year falls on one date or carries the same narrative. |
+| BANK-004-158 | What distinguishes an Ashta Lakshmi grouping from one universal eight-form list? | Compare a specified public temple or textual system, names and attributes; label regional variation and do not impose one image's objects on all Lakshmi forms. |
+| BANK-004-159 | How can a Panchamukhi Hanuman illustration identify its five faces without conflating regional arrangements? | Choose a documented public iconographic reference, record orientation and attributes, and distinguish the selected convention from other depictions; exclude restricted ritual material. |
+| BANK-004-160 | How do Ardhanarishvara images encode the two sides through clothing, gesture and companions? | Inspect named dated images with museum or temple documentation and compare a public iconographic text; separate observed details from features reconstructed by a modern artist. |
