+# 006 Science & Big Questions: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**23 categories · 119 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Science & Big Questions. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Models and measurement
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-013 | Why is a scientific model useful even when it leaves things out? | Compare a model's purpose, assumptions, predictions and failure range using a worked example rather than demanding a complete replica of reality. |
+| BANK-006-014 | What separates a measurement from an interpretation of that measurement? | Trace instrument response, calibration, processing and theoretical inference in one actual experiment. |
+| BANK-006-015 | How do confidence intervals differ from the probability that a theory is true? | Use repeated-sampling interpretation and distinguish parameter uncertainty from uncertainty about assumptions or models. |
+| BANK-006-016 | Why does a highly precise result still need a check for systematic error? | Compare random variation with calibration and model bias; use a case with explicit measurement procedures. |
+| BANK-006-017 | What would make a scientific question currently unanswerable rather than meaningless? | Distinguish inaccessible observations, inadequate instruments and claims with no testable implications. |
+
+## 02. Matter and quantum questions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-018 | What does the Higgs mechanism explain about mass, and what does it not explain? | Separate elementary-particle masses from composite-particle mass and avoid reducing all mass to one interaction. |
+| BANK-006-019 | What is directly measured in a double-slit experiment? | Distinguish detection events, interference patterns and the claims added by competing interpretations. |
+| BANK-006-020 | How do entanglement experiments test local hidden-variable accounts? | Explain a specified test, assumptions and loopholes without presenting correlations as faster-than-light messaging. |
+| BANK-006-021 | Why is a quantum superposition not simply an ordinary mixture of unknown alternatives? | Compare preparations and observable interference using a defined two-state system. |
+| BANK-006-022 | What makes quantum gravity difficult to test experimentally? | Compare relevant scales, candidate observations and the gap between mathematical consistency and empirical support. |
+
+## 03. Space, gravity and time
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-023 | How can clocks measure different elapsed times without either clock malfunctioning? | Compare a documented relativity experiment, paths and reference frames rather than invoking vague subjective time. |
+| BANK-006-024 | What observations distinguish an expanding universe from galaxies merely moving through fixed space? | Use redshift-distance evidence and cosmological models while identifying assumptions and local-motion complications. |
+| BANK-006-025 | What does gravitational-wave detection actually record? | Trace detector signals, noise rejection, independent observations and model-based parameter estimation. |
+| BANK-006-026 | How can observations support a black hole without showing its interior? | Compare orbital motion, radiation, gravitational waves and imaging; distinguish evidence for an object from claims about unobserved interiors. |
+| BANK-006-027 | Why does entropy enter explanations of the arrow of time? | Separate microscopic laws, statistical descriptions, initial conditions and unresolved philosophical interpretation. |
+
+## 04. Dark components and cosmic history
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-028 | Which observations motivate dark matter as more than a galaxy-rotation hypothesis? | Compare independent evidence channels and distinguish successful prediction from direct identification of a particle. |
+| BANK-006-029 | What would count as a credible direct-detection signal for dark matter? | Inspect backgrounds, detector response, replication and compatibility with other searches. |
+| BANK-006-030 | How do researchers infer accelerated cosmic expansion? | Compare distance indicators, model assumptions and systematic uncertainties without describing dark energy as a fully understood substance. |
+| BANK-006-031 | What does the cosmic microwave background reveal about early conditions? | Separate measured temperature patterns from model-dependent estimates and the limits of observing earlier epochs. |
+| BANK-006-032 | How can measurements of the expansion rate disagree without proving that all cosmology has failed? | Compare methods, calibrations, uncertainties and possible theoretical explanations before choosing a conclusion. |
+
+## 05. Life's origins and definitions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-033 | What distinguishes evidence about life's chemistry from a complete origin-of-life explanation? | Compare laboratory pathways, environmental plausibility and missing links between molecules, compartments and heredity. |
+| BANK-006-034 | How do protocell experiments test ideas about early life? | Identify what the constructed system does, what researchers supply and which claims cannot be generalized to ancient Earth. |
+| BANK-006-035 | Why is there no single definition of life accepted for every scientific purpose? | Compare metabolism, replication, evolution and borderline cases while making the chosen definition explicit. |
+| BANK-006-036 | What evidence supports endosymbiotic origins of major cellular components? | Compare genomes, membranes, cellular structures and alternative historical explanations. |
+| BANK-006-037 | How can the search for extraterrestrial life avoid assuming Earth chemistry is universal? | Distinguish practical detection targets, alternative hypotheses and limitations imposed by current instruments. |
+
+## 06. Evolution and complexity
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-038 | How can complexity evolve without evolution aiming toward greater complexity? | Compare selection, drift, duplication, cooperation and simplification in specific documented cases. |
+| BANK-006-039 | What evidence separates natural selection from genetic drift in a population? | Inspect variation, population size, fitness evidence and statistical uncertainty rather than inferring adaptation from usefulness alone. |
+| BANK-006-040 | How do researchers study major transitions such as multicellularity? | Compare fossils, comparative biology and experiments while separating independent origins and different definitions of transition. |
+| BANK-006-041 | Why can similar features evolve independently in distant lineages? | Use a documented convergence example and distinguish common constraints from proof of identical evolutionary paths. |
+| BANK-006-042 | What does a phylogenetic tree establish about relationships rather than progress? | Explain branching, uncertainty, sampling and the difference between living relatives and direct ancestors. |
+
+## 07. Mind and consciousness
