+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-043 | What can a neural correlate of consciousness establish without explaining experience? | Distinguish association, necessity, sufficiency and interpretation within one experimental paradigm. |
+| BANK-006-044 | How do experiments separate attention from conscious awareness? | Compare task demands, report requirements and competing explanations of an observed effect. |
+| BANK-006-045 | What makes reports of an altered state difficult to compare across participants? | Examine vocabulary, expectations, measurement timing and the distinction between experience and later interpretation. |
+| BANK-006-046 | Can a system's convincing report of awareness establish subjective experience? | Compare behavioral evidence, philosophical assumptions and competing theories without declaring one test decisive. |
+| BANK-006-047 | Why do theories of consciousness disagree about what should be measured? | Identify their proposed mechanisms, predictions and the degree to which tests can distinguish them. |
+
+## 08. Earth, energy and limits
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-048 | Why does renewable energy still involve physical and material constraints? | Compare variability, storage, transmission, land and lifecycle assumptions without treating one limitation as proof of impossibility. |
+| BANK-006-049 | What distinguishes a climate model projection from a weather forecast? | Compare questions, time scales, initial conditions, scenarios and statistical validation. |
+| BANK-006-050 | How do mass extinctions change ecosystems beyond simply reducing species counts? | Use a bounded fossil interval to examine selectivity, recovery and changes in ecological relationships. |
+| BANK-006-051 | What does carrying capacity mean when technology and consumption change? | Separate a fixed toy model from real systems with feedback, distribution and changing resource use. |
+| BANK-006-052 | How should a science channel explain uncertainty without implying ignorance about everything? | Distinguish well-supported mechanisms, parameter ranges, model limits and genuinely open questions in one case. |
+
+## 09. Thermodynamics and information
+
