+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-006-053 | How does a heat engine's efficiency depend on where heat can flow? | Use primary physical definitions and an illustrative cycle; distinguish ideal limits from actual machines. |
+| BANK-006-054 | What does entropy measure in a specified physical system? | Compare microscopic descriptions and thermodynamic variables without reducing entropy to visual mess. |
+| BANK-006-055 | Why does erasing information raise a physical question about energy? | Review original information-thermodynamics work and explicit assumptions. |
+| BANK-006-056 | How can local order increase while total entropy still rises? | Track energy and system boundaries in a bounded physical example. |
+| BANK-006-057 | What distinguishes reversible equations from irreversible everyday processes? | Compare microscopic models, coarse graining and initial conditions. |
+| BANK-006-058 | How should a science video separate thermodynamic entropy from an analogy about society? | Identify mathematical definitions and where the analogy stops. |
+
