+# 007 AI Tools / AI Tutorials: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**21 categories · 104 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for AI Tools / AI Tutorials. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Choosing and testing tools
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-007-013 | How can a creator turn an AI tool comparison into a repeatable test? | Define the task, input set, success criteria, versions, settings and failure log before selecting attractive examples. |
+| BANK-007-014 | What does a free AI plan actually allow a complete workflow to finish? | Test quotas, exports, watermarks, commercial terms and repeat attempts on a dated plan rather than comparing only advertised access. |
+| BANK-007-015 | When is a local AI tool a practical alternative to a cloud service? | Compare actual hardware, setup effort, privacy, quality, maintenance and end-to-end time on the same task. |
+| BANK-007-016 | How should a tutorial record model and application versions? | Preserve settings, dates, interface changes and reproducible inputs so viewers can identify why their results differ. |
+| BANK-007-017 | What makes an AI-generated example cherry-picked? | Report attempts, rejected outputs and selection criteria; distinguish illustrative success from representative performance. |
+
+## 02. Writing and document workflows
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
