+# 021 Luxury / Rich Lifestyle: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Luxury / Rich Lifestyle. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Defining luxury
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-013 | How has the meaning of luxury changed across periods and social groups? | Compare named historical settings, consumption and access rather than presenting one timeless expensive lifestyle. |
+| BANK-021-014 | What separates craftsmanship, scarcity and branding in a luxury price? | Trace a specific product's documented materials, labor, distribution and marketing; avoid inferring cost from its retail price. |
+| BANK-021-015 | When does ownership communicate status differently from temporary access? | Compare leasing, rental, membership and purchase in a defined market without assuming identical motives among buyers. |
+| BANK-021-016 | How can a luxury documentary distinguish an advertisement from an independent investigation? | Disclose access conditions, sponsorship and editorial limits alongside the actual evidence gathered. |
+
+## 02. Private aviation
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-017 | When does private-jet ownership cost more than chartering for the same travel pattern? | Include utilization, crew, hangar, maintenance, repositioning and financing in a transparent illustrative comparison. |
+| BANK-021-018 | What does a charter quote omit unless its terms are inspected? | Check positioning, taxes, waiting, cancellation, baggage and weather contingencies for a particular operator and date. |
+| BANK-021-019 | Why can two private aircraft with similar cabin capacity have different operating economics? | Compare range, mission, maintenance cycles, utilization and airport constraints rather than purchase price alone. |
+| BANK-021-020 | What does a private-aviation tour reveal about service labor behind the cabin? | Include scheduling, ground handling, catering and crew work instead of depicting service as automatic abundance. |
+
+## 03. Yachts and high-cost assets
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-021 | How does a yacht's annual operating budget depend on its actual use? | Separate crew, berth, fuel, insurance, surveys and refit under a defined operating scenario. |
+| BANK-021-022 | What can a marine survey establish before a yacht purchase? | Distinguish visible condition, inspection access, tests and excluded systems; do not treat a survey as a guarantee. |
+| BANK-021-023 | How do superyacht interiors balance appearance with maritime requirements? | Compare weight, materials, fire protection and maintenance access using documented design constraints. |
+| BANK-021-024 | When does charter revenue fail to cover a vessel's full ownership cost? | Include utilization, commissions, downtime, servicing and depreciation rather than gross booking income alone. |
+
+## 04. Watches and craft
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-025 | What makes a mechanical watch complication technically distinct from decoration? | Use a documented movement to trace function, components and servicing rather than relying on prestige language. |
+| BANK-021-026 | How can hand finishing be evaluated without confusing it with timekeeping accuracy? | Separate surface work, manufacture, regulation and testing; compare observable features with stated claims. |
+| BANK-021-027 | Why do provenance and replacement parts matter in a vintage watch? | Trace serial records, service history and disclosed changes before comparing market values. |
+| BANK-021-028 | What does a watch's water-resistance rating mean under its actual testing standard? | Check specified conditions, age and servicing; avoid presenting a rating as universal suitability for every activity. |
+
+## 05. Fashion, jewelry and materials
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-029 | How does haute couture production differ from a luxury ready-to-wear label? | Compare actual institutional definitions, fitting, production and client process in a named fashion context. |
+| BANK-021-030 | What evidence supports the provenance of a high-value gemstone? | Distinguish origin reports, treatment disclosure, ownership history and the limits of each document. |
+| BANK-021-031 | When does a luxury material's visual quality say little about its durability? | Compare intended use, testing, maintenance and repair rather than treating price as a performance measure. |
+| BANK-021-032 | How can artisan work be credited in a brand-centered product story? | Identify workshops, skills, labor and contractual visibility without assuming the designer's name represents all production. |
+
+## 06. Service and hospitality
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-033 | What does a premium hotel stay depend on beyond visible amenities? | Trace housekeeping, maintenance, scheduling and service recovery with staff perspectives and guest consent. |
+| BANK-021-034 | How do concierge promises change when a request depends on third parties? | Separate arranged access, availability, fees and actual authority rather than implying unlimited influence. |
+| BANK-021-035 | What makes personalized service different from intrusive data collection? | Compare guest choice, recorded preferences, retention and access to personal information in a specific property. |
+| BANK-021-036 | How can a resort's sustainability claim be checked against its operations? | Inspect water, energy, sourcing, labor and local effects rather than accepting a polished tour as evidence. |
+
+## 07. Markets and resale
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-037 | Why can a luxury item's resale price differ sharply from its original retail price? | Compare condition, supply, transaction fees, authentication and changing demand using dated sales evidence. |
+| BANK-021-038 | How do waitlists and allocation rules shape perceptions of scarcity? | Distinguish actual production limits, distribution choices and unverifiable customer anecdotes. |
+| BANK-021-039 | What can an authentication service establish about a luxury object? | Check methods, scope, limitations and liability; avoid treating one certificate as a complete ownership history. |
+| BANK-021-040 | How should a video compare luxury purchases as investments? | Include costs, liquidity, selection bias and failed examples rather than highlighting only appreciated objects. |
+
+## 08. Cultural and ethical interpretation
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-021-041 | How can a wealth profile explain access without inventing a person's net worth? | Use reliable disclosures, asset ownership limits and uncertainty rather than assigning value from photographs. |
+| BANK-021-042 | What is lost when luxury media presents consumption as proof of merit? | Examine inheritance, labor, institutions and different values without assuming identical life histories. |
+| BANK-021-043 | How can a film show elite spaces without turning workers into anonymous scenery? | Include consent, agency and the labor systems that make the experience possible. |
+| BANK-021-044 | When does a luxury tour's exclusivity claim need independent checking? | Verify access terms, comparable alternatives and sponsorship before repeating a superlative. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
