+# 022 Cars / Automotive Stories: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Cars / Automotive Stories. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Vehicle stories and evidence
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-013 | How did assembly-line production change more than the speed of car building? | Compare labor, parts standardization, pricing and distribution in a bounded manufacturing history. |
+| BANK-022-014 | Why do automotive origin stories often credit one inventor for a larger system? | Trace component development, patents, suppliers and adoption rather than a single heroic date. |
+| BANK-022-015 | How did Japanese kei-car rules shape actual vehicle design? | Use dated regulations and model specifications to connect dimensions, performance and intended use. |
+| BANK-022-016 | What does an archived advertisement reveal about a car beyond its engineering? | Compare claimed audiences, values and features with independent records of ownership and performance. |
+
+## 02. Engines and powertrains
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-017 | What changed when fuel injection replaced carburetion in a named vehicle family? | Compare control, emissions, starting, service and period requirements rather than treating the transition as one instantaneous improvement. |
+| BANK-022-018 | How does turbocharging alter a powertrain's thermal and response tradeoffs? | Trace a documented system, load conditions and control strategy without equating boost with free power. |
+| BANK-022-019 | Why can engines with similar displacement deliver different driving characteristics? | Compare architecture, tuning, forced induction, gearing and vehicle load using matched conditions. |
+| BANK-022-020 | What does a transmission's gear count conceal about its actual behavior? | Examine ratios, control, efficiency, response and the vehicle's use rather than ranking by the largest number. |
+
+## 03. Chassis and vehicle dynamics
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-021 | How do suspension design and tuning answer different engineering questions? | Separate layout, geometry, damping and intended use using a specific vehicle example. |
+| BANK-022-022 | What makes all-wheel-drive systems differ under the same marketing label? | Compare torque paths, control, operating conditions and limitations rather than assuming constant equal drive to every wheel. |
+| BANK-022-023 | How can tires change a vehicle comparison more than a visible styling feature? | Match specifications, conditions and wear; separate measured grip, comfort and rolling resistance. |
+| BANK-022-024 | Why does adding vehicle weight change more than acceleration? | Trace braking, load capacity, tires, energy use and control assumptions without reducing behavior to one ratio. |
+
+## 04. Aerodynamics and packaging
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-025 | How can a car's aerodynamic needs conflict with cooling and cabin space? | Compare actual airflow paths, heat rejection, dimensions and measured drag rather than appearance alone. |
+| BANK-022-026 | What does a quoted drag coefficient omit without frontal area and conditions? | Show the relevant quantities and testing context before comparing total aerodynamic resistance. |
+| BANK-022-027 | How do electric platforms change passenger and luggage packaging? | Separate battery placement, structure, crash constraints and vehicle dimensions in a matched example. |
+| BANK-022-028 | When does a concept car's visual design fail to establish production feasibility? | Inspect access, visibility, cooling, structure and manufacturing details absent from a display prototype. |
+
+## 05. Safety and testing
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-029 | How should crash-test ratings be compared across years and protocols? | Align procedures, vehicle categories, equipment and scoring rather than ranking old and new stars directly. |
+| BANK-022-030 | What can driver-assistance testing establish without proving full autonomy? | Specify operational conditions, supervision, failure handling and the distinction between marketing and actual function. |
+| BANK-022-031 | Why can a safety recall matter even if most owners have not observed a fault? | Explain defect conditions, exposure and remedy using the actual manufacturer or regulator notice. |
+| BANK-022-032 | How can an incident investigation distinguish a design issue from other contributing factors? | Use the documented evidence and uncertainty without assigning causation from an isolated video. |
+
+## 06. Industry and manufacturing
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-033 | How does platform sharing affect cars sold under different brands? | Compare components, calibration, manufacturing and service while preserving meaningful differences. |
+| BANK-022-034 | Why can a factory shutdown spread through a supplier network? | Trace inventory, unique components, alternatives and lead times in a documented disruption. |
+| BANK-022-035 | What does localization mean when a vehicle includes globally sourced systems? | Separate assembly, component manufacture, design and ownership rather than using one national label as a complete description. |
+| BANK-022-036 | How should a brand revival be evaluated beyond a familiar badge? | Compare product engineering, ownership, manufacturing and support with the earlier company history. |
+
+## 07. Ownership and repair
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-037 | What belongs in a car's total cost of ownership? | Include depreciation, financing, energy, insurance, taxes, service and scenario-specific use rather than purchase price alone. |
+| BANK-022-038 | When does a low-mileage used car still require costly maintenance? | Inspect age, storage, service history, consumables and actual condition without universal mileage rules. |
+| BANK-022-039 | How can parts availability determine whether a vehicle remains practical to own? | Compare supply, compatible substitutes, diagnostic tools and repair expertise for a named model. |
+| BANK-022-040 | What does a used-car inspection establish and leave uncertain? | Define access, tests, records and exclusions rather than representing inspection as a guarantee. |
+
+## 08. Automotive media literacy
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-022-041 | How can a road test separate measured performance from the reviewer's preference? | State conditions, instruments and judgments clearly; avoid presenting subjective feel as a universal result. |
+| BANK-022-042 | What should be disclosed when a manufacturer supplies a test vehicle? | Identify travel, access, sponsorship and editorial conditions alongside independent checks. |
+| BANK-022-043 | How can historic car footage be misleading when later modifications are present? | Check configuration, period equipment, restoration and labels rather than treating every running example as original. |
+| BANK-022-044 | Why should fastest-car claims specify category and verification conditions? | Separate production status, route, direction, timing and independent evidence before repeating a record. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
