+# 023 Spirituality / Meditation: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Spirituality / Meditation. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Meanings of spiritual practice
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-013 | How do spiritual and secular meditation programs define different aims? | Compare named sources and curricula without assuming identical exercises imply identical meanings. |
+| BANK-023-014 | What does a spiritual experience report establish about the reporter's interpretation? | Separate experience, later explanation, community vocabulary and independently testable claims. |
+| BANK-023-015 | How do traditions distinguish belief, practice and realization? | Use attributed teachings rather than imposing one universal ladder of spiritual progress. |
+| BANK-023-016 | Why can the same word for awareness mean different things in different schools? | Compare original terms, translations and philosophical context before equating them. |
+
+## 02. Teachers and authority
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-017 | How is a teacher's authority recognized in a named spiritual institution? | Compare lineage, training, community recognition and actual accountability rather than accepting a title alone. |
+| BANK-023-018 | What changes when a private teaching relationship becomes a large online audience? | Examine access, personalization, responsibility and the limits of interpreting public content as individual guidance. |
+| BANK-023-019 | How can students question a teaching without being treated as disloyal? | Use documented community policies and participant accounts; preserve differences rather than portraying one universal response. |
+| BANK-023-020 | What should be distinguished between spiritual teaching and professional mental-health care? | Clarify roles, qualifications, consent and referral boundaries without diagnosing an individual or dismissing their beliefs. |
+
+## 03. Retreats and daily life
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-021 | How does retreat practice differ from meditation in a busy household? | Compare support, schedule, obligations and participation rather than treating duration as the only difference. |
+| BANK-023-022 | What should a retreat disclose before enrollment? | Inspect activities, costs, screening, accessibility, withdrawal options and support using actual published terms. |
+| BANK-023-023 | How can a household spiritual routine adapt when care responsibilities change? | Document participant choices, values and resources instead of prescribing an inflexible ideal schedule. |
+| BANK-023-024 | What does silence mean in one community's observance? | Compare purpose, duration, communication exceptions and participants' own interpretations. |
+
+## 04. Experience and expectation
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-025 | How can expectations shape reports of a meditation experience? | Inspect instruction, prior belief, measurement and alternative explanations without denying the person's experience. |
+| BANK-023-026 | Why is an unusual sensation insufficient evidence of spiritual attainment? | Distinguish subjective reports, doctrinal interpretation and the absence of a universal objective attainment measure. |
+| BANK-023-027 | What can interviews capture about practice that a minutes-per-day log misses? | Explore meaning, context, difficulty and change while acknowledging sampling and retrospective limits. |
+| BANK-023-028 | How can comparison with exceptional practitioners distort a beginner's expectations? | Examine selection, edited stories and differences in goals rather than treating rare reports as a required outcome. |
+
+## 05. Ethics and belonging
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-029 | How can spiritual communities provide belonging while preserving personal autonomy? | Compare participation choices, disagreement, privacy and exit conditions in a named setting. |
+| BANK-023-030 | What happens when a spiritual explanation prevents a practical problem from being addressed? | Use a consented or clearly illustrative case and distinguish interpretation from avoidance without diagnosing beliefs. |
+| BANK-023-031 | How can service and contemplation relate in a specific tradition? | Read attributed teachings and participant accounts rather than assuming withdrawal from society is the universal ideal. |
+| BANK-023-032 | What does meaningful consent require in emotionally vulnerable group activities? | Inspect disclosure, pressure, opt-outs and support rather than treating attendance as blanket agreement. |
+
+## 06. Commercial spirituality
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-033 | How should a paid spiritual course's promises be evaluated? | Compare actual content, costs, qualifications, refund terms and claims that cannot be independently guaranteed. |
+| BANK-023-034 | What changes when spiritual progress is sold as a measurable product? | Examine defined outcomes, evidence and commercial incentives without assuming payment alone invalidates a tradition. |
+| BANK-023-035 | How can a creator disclose sponsorship of a retreat or wellness program? | Separate compensation, access and evidence from personal testimony in the resulting review. |
+| BANK-023-036 | Why should claims of universal healing require different evidence from accounts of personal meaning? | Distinguish spiritual testimony, measured health outcomes and professional boundaries. |
+
+## 07. Texts and translations
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-037 | How can a short spiritual quotation reverse the meaning of its source passage? | Read the surrounding argument, translator choices and intended audience before using it as general advice. |
+| BANK-023-038 | What does self-inquiry mean in a named teacher's recorded teachings? | Compare authorized editions and context; avoid reducing a dialogical practice to a generic slogan. |
+| BANK-023-039 | How can modern mindfulness language reshape a traditional contemplative term? | Trace source, commentary and secular curriculum rather than assuming exact equivalence. |
+| BANK-023-040 | Why should comparative spirituality preserve disagreement rather than declare all traditions identical? | Compare aims, authority and self concepts with attribution and explicit limits. |
+
+## 08. Documentary responsibility
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-023-041 | How can a film portray contemplative depth without staging enlightenment? | Use observable practice, consented interpretation and sourced context rather than synthetic proof of attainment. |
+| BANK-023-042 | What should be disclosed when a spiritual testimony is edited? | Preserve qualifiers, chronology and relevant context; distinguish one person's account from a representative finding. |
+| BANK-023-043 | How can a channel cover criticism of a spiritual institution fairly? | Use verified public evidence, responses and careful attribution; avoid unsupported allegations about identifiable people. |
+| BANK-023-044 | Which topics belong in a general spirituality bank rather than the detailed meditation-method bank? | Keep meaning, community and interpretation here; route method-specific textual and experimental depth to niche 278. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
