+# 025 Gaming Stories / Lore: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Gaming Stories / Lore. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Canon and sources
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-013 | How can a lore video distinguish official canon from fan interpretation? | Track game version, in-game evidence, developer statements and licensed material rather than grouping all claims together. |
+| BANK-025-014 | What changes when a live-service update revises earlier lore? | Compare dated text, events and patches; distinguish contradiction, retcon and new perspective where evidence allows. |
+| BANK-025-015 | How should an unreliable in-game narrator be treated as a source? | Compare motives, knowledge and corroboration rather than accepting every written account as world fact. |
+| BANK-025-016 | What does a developer interview establish when it conflicts with the released game? | State the sources, dates and interpretive choices without pretending authorial intent removes all ambiguity. |
+
+## 02. Environmental storytelling
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-017 | How can architecture communicate a game's past without a narrator? | Analyze a specific location's layout, objects and traversal alongside the evidence for the proposed history. |
+| BANK-025-018 | What makes item placement a meaningful clue rather than decorative repetition? | Compare consistency, interaction and context; acknowledge alternative production explanations. |
+| BANK-025-019 | How does enemy placement shape a player's understanding of a fallen society? | Distinguish observed design from inferred narrative and avoid treating every mechanic as literal historical evidence. |
+| BANK-025-020 | How can a lore analysis use silence and absence responsibly? | Define what the game leads players to expect before treating missing content as intentional proof. |
+
+## 03. Narrative systems
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-021 | How do branching dialogue states preserve continuity across player choices? | Trace flags, dependencies and outcomes in a documented or illustrative system without conflating all branches into one canon. |
+| BANK-025-022 | What makes a quest's mechanical reward reinforce or undermine its story? | Compare intended choices, incentives and actual outcomes through a bounded quest analysis. |
+| BANK-025-023 | How can faction reputation produce different accounts of the same event? | Separate variable game states, character viewpoints and shared underlying events. |
+| BANK-025-024 | What should a narrative database track when a world spans several releases? | Include chronology, provenance, variants and unresolved contradictions rather than one unqualified summary per character. |
+
+## 04. World history and interpretation
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-025 | How can Elder Scrolls in-game texts support competing historical readings? | Select actual texts, versions and contradictions; distinguish the analysis from a claim that every account is equally reliable. |
+| BANK-025-026 | What makes a Dark Souls environmental interpretation testable against the game? | Connect location, description and encounter evidence; state where a theory depends on speculation. |
+| BANK-025-027 | How should a game inspired by mythology be compared with its source tradition? | Identify the chosen works and deliberate adaptations rather than treating fictional mechanics as authentic theology. |
+| BANK-025-028 | What can localization change about a world's implied history? | Compare source and translated wording with version and context before claiming a mistranslation. |
+
+## 05. Player agency and canon
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-029 | When does a player choice change the narrative rather than only its presentation? | Trace consequences, dialogue and later states instead of relying on the number of displayed options. |
+| BANK-025-030 | How can a sequel select one outcome without erasing earlier player experiences? | Compare continuity policy, released material and the difference between a player's playthrough and official continuation. |
+| BANK-025-031 | What happens when gameplay time conflicts with story chronology? | Separate abstraction, repeated mechanics and explicit narrative dates using specific examples. |
+| BANK-025-032 | How can a video explain multiple endings without implying they all occur sequentially? | Use branching structure, conditions and source labels rather than one flattened timeline. |
+
+## 06. Sound and visual language
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-033 | How can a recurring musical motif suggest a relationship between characters? | Compare actual cues and contexts; distinguish observed recurrence from unsupported claims about composer intent. |
+| BANK-025-034 | What makes a faction's visual identity readable across different environments? | Analyze shapes, materials, colors and exceptions rather than assigning meaning from one screenshot. |
+| BANK-025-035 | How do camera and interface choices control what the player can know? | Separate restricted information, unreliable display and ordinary technical limits in a bounded sequence. |
+| BANK-025-036 | When does a cinematic trailer misrepresent the story available in the game? | Compare promotional footage with released scenes, mechanics and disclosed production status. |
+
+## 07. Communities and preservation
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-037 | How do fan theories become accepted lore through repetition? | Trace sources, copied wording and later corrections rather than treating popularity as corroboration. |
+| BANK-025-038 | What is lost when a delisted game or event can no longer be played? | Examine recordings, builds, legal access, player archives and limits on reconstructing the original experience. |
+| BANK-025-039 | How can a lore creator credit community discoveries? | Track original posts, contributors, verification and permission rather than presenting collected work as solitary discovery. |
+| BANK-025-040 | What should a video do when a mod changes the evidence it analyzes? | Identify modifications, version and affected assets so viewers can separate base-game content from additions. |
+
+## 08. Responsible episode design
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-025-041 | How can a long lore timeline remain understandable without hiding uncertainty? | Separate confirmed events, approximate ordering and disputed accounts with clear labels and navigation. |
+| BANK-025-042 | What makes a spoiler warning useful rather than a vague opening phrase? | State the game, release, chapters and ending content covered without revealing the spoiler itself. |
+| BANK-025-043 | How should synthetic voices or reconstructed game footage be disclosed? | Distinguish generated explanation, modded scenes and actual captured evidence; respect voice and asset rights. |
+| BANK-025-044 | What should change when an update invalidates a lore video's conclusion? | Add dated corrections, explain the revised evidence and preserve the distinction between old and current versions. |
