+# 030 Earth & Natural Mysteries: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Earth & Natural Mysteries. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Investigating a natural mystery
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-013 | What turns an unusual natural event into a testable question? | Define observations, conditions, measurement and alternative explanations rather than using unexplained as evidence for a preferred cause. |
+| BANK-030-014 | How can a striking video misrepresent the frequency of a natural phenomenon? | Examine selection, location, timing and repeated events instead of inferring rarity from one viral clip. |
+| BANK-030-015 | Why is a plausible physical explanation insufficient without evidence from the actual site? | Compare general mechanism, local conditions and observations that could distinguish alternatives. |
+| BANK-030-016 | What should a field investigation record before trying to solve a mystery? | Preserve time, location, instruments, weather, context and uncertainty without disturbing the relevant evidence. |
+
+## 02. Moving landscapes
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-017 | How were moving stones on a dry lakebed investigated? | Compare observed tracks, weather, water or ice conditions and direct monitoring rather than relying on visual speculation. |
+| BANK-030-018 | What causes a river to abandon one channel for another? | Examine sediment, slope, floods and human alterations in a bounded case rather than a single universal trigger. |
+| BANK-030-019 | How can dunes appear stationary while individual grains move? | Distinguish transport, landform migration, time scale and observation method. |
+| BANK-030-020 | What can an erratic boulder reveal about a landscape's past? | Compare rock provenance, transport hypotheses and dating without inferring a precise route from location alone. |
+
+## 03. Hidden water and ground failure
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-021 | How does karst geology create some sinkholes? | Trace rock, groundwater and ground conditions while distinguishing different collapse mechanisms. |
+| BANK-030-022 | What does a disappearing stream reveal about subsurface flow? | Use geological context and appropriate tracing evidence rather than assuming a visible outlet connects directly. |
+| BANK-030-023 | How can a lake release dangerous gas without a conventional volcanic eruption? | Explain a documented mechanism, stratification and evidence; preserve the boundary between explanation and personal safety guidance. |
+| BANK-030-024 | Why can groundwater changes alter a landscape far from a visible river? | Compare aquifers, pumping, geology and measured movement rather than treating the subsurface as one open reservoir. |
+
+## 04. Atmospheric appearances
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-025 | How does a mirage change the apparent position of an object? | Trace refraction and temperature gradients while separating the optical image from an actual displaced object. |
+| BANK-030-026 | Why can a lenticular cloud seem fixed while air moves through it? | Explain wave conditions and condensation with observations rather than identifying cloud shape alone as proof of one cause. |
+| BANK-030-027 | What are sprites above thunderstorms, and how are they observed? | Distinguish high-altitude optical events, instruments and timing from ordinary ground lightning. |
+| BANK-030-028 | Why is ball-lightning evidence difficult to evaluate? | Compare reports, instrument records, laboratory analogies and limits on matching proposed mechanisms to observations. |
+
+## 05. Unusual surfaces and structures
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-029 | How can polygonal ground patterns form under different conditions? | Compare thermal contraction, drying, materials and scale rather than assigning one origin from shape alone. |
+| BANK-030-030 | What makes desert varnish a continuing research question? | Inspect composition, environment, biological proposals and formation-rate uncertainty without claiming one settled universal process. |
+| BANK-030-031 | How do columnar rock structures reveal cooling and fracture? | Compare material, geometry and formation evidence while distinguishing visual resemblance from identical geological history. |
+| BANK-030-032 | What can concentric rock patterns reveal about weathering or structure? | Use geological mapping, scale and alternative explanations rather than treating a circular image as proof of an impact. |
+
+## 06. Magnetic and gravity claims
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-033 | Why can a road appear to slope uphill when an object rolls downhill? | Compare measured gradient, horizon cues and visual reference rather than attributing motion to an unmeasured force. |
+| BANK-030-034 | How should a claim of unusual magnetism at a tourist site be tested? | Specify instruments, controls, location and field measurements; avoid inferring magnetism from a compass video alone. |
+| BANK-030-035 | What does a local gravity anomaly mean scientifically? | Explain reference models, measurement and geology without equating a small deviation with an impossible landscape. |
+| BANK-030-036 | How can consumer navigation errors create a false geographic mystery? | Inspect coordinates, maps, sensor limitations and metadata before assigning an environmental cause. |
+
+## 07. Famous mystery narratives
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-037 | What does a fair investigation of Bermuda Triangle incidents need to count? | Define boundaries, time, traffic exposure, inclusion criteria and known causes rather than collecting only striking disappearances. |
+| BANK-030-038 | How can an old natural-disaster account combine observation and later embellishment? | Trace contemporary witnesses, repeated claims and changing interpretations with a clear chronology. |
+| BANK-030-039 | Why do natural alignments attract intentional-design claims? | Compare pattern selection, chance, geology and independent evidence of human intervention. |
+| BANK-030-040 | What would justify saying an unusual event remains unexplained? | State which observations are reliable, which mechanisms were tested and which missing data prevent resolution. |
+
+## 08. Visual explanation and correction
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-030-041 | How can an animation explain a natural mechanism without pretending to reproduce the exact event? | Label illustrative parameters, simplify transparently and distinguish observed data from reconstructed motion. |
+| BANK-030-042 | What should change when a spectacular natural-mystery claim is debunked? | Correct the central claim, explain the evidence and update titles or images that still imply the false version. |
+| BANK-030-043 | How can a field episode include local knowledge without treating all testimony as measurement? | Attribute accounts respectfully and compare them with recorded observations and uncertainty. |
+| BANK-030-044 | Why should a science channel preserve wonder after offering an ordinary explanation? | Show the actual mechanism's complexity and evidence rather than treating understanding as the end of curiosity. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
