+## 01. Scale and engineering decisions
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-031-013 | What makes a structure a megaproject beyond its physical size? | Compare cost, interfaces, schedule, uncertainty and institutional coordination rather than using one height or length threshold. |
+| BANK-031-014 | How does an engineering requirement become a design constraint? | Trace a specific project's loads, access, environment and operating purpose before comparing proposed forms. |
+| BANK-031-015 | Why can an elegant concept fail during construction planning? | Inspect sequence, temporary support, delivery access and tolerances instead of judging only the finished structure. |
+| BANK-031-016 | What should a megastructure visualization label as proposed rather than built? | Separate renderings, approved design, active construction and completed operation with dated project evidence. |
+
+## 02. Bridges and long spans
+
