+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-031-017 | How do suspension and cable-stayed bridges distribute loads differently? | Compare documented load paths, geometry and site requirements without ranking forms independent of their setting. |
+| BANK-031-018 | Why can wind govern a long-span bridge's shape? | Explain aerodynamic response, testing and damping using a specific study rather than an isolated dramatic failure clip. |
+| BANK-031-019 | How do builders connect bridge segments before the final load path exists? | Trace a documented erection sequence, temporary stability and survey control. |
+| BANK-031-020 | What can foundation scour change even when a bridge deck appears sound? | Connect water flow, sediment, foundations and inspection evidence without diagnosing a structure from photographs. |
