+## 07. Cost, risk and institutions
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-031-037 | Why do megaproject cost estimates change as a design becomes better defined? | Separate scope growth, uncertainty, inflation, optimism and procurement changes using dated estimates. |
+| BANK-031-038 | What distinguishes contingency from permission to exceed a budget? | Explain risk allocation, approval and reporting within a named project's governance. |
+| BANK-031-039 | How should claimed economic benefits be compared with observed outcomes? | Align forecasts, usage, alternatives, time horizon and distribution rather than equating completion with success. |
+| BANK-031-040 | Who bears a megaproject's costs when benefits accrue elsewhere? | Compare displacement, public finance, access and affected communities through documented perspectives. |
+
+## 08. Operations and lifecycle
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-031-041 | How does maintenance access shape the life of a large structure? | Use inspection routes, replaceable components and operating closures rather than the construction spectacle alone. |
+| BANK-031-042 | What changes when a megastructure outlives its original purpose? | Compare adaptation, decommissioning, financing and environmental obligations in a real case. |
+| BANK-031-043 | How can a documentary distinguish record-breaking size from useful capacity? | State the measurement category, actual service and constraints instead of ranking by superlatives alone. |
+| BANK-031-044 | What should a project film revisit years after the opening ceremony? | Compare maintenance, use, costs and community outcomes with its original promises. |
