+# 033 UFO / Extraterrestrial: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for UFO / Extraterrestrial. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Claims and evidence categories
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-013 | What does unidentified mean in an official aerial-observation report? | Distinguish insufficient data, unresolved classification and evidence for a specific extraordinary explanation. |
+| BANK-033-014 | How can a report's authenticity differ from the truth of every interpretation attached to it? | Separate document provenance, recorded observation and causal inference. |
+| BANK-033-015 | What should be preserved when evaluating an unusual aerial video? | Inspect original file, time, location, sensor information and editing history before interpreting motion. |
+| BANK-033-016 | Why can several witnesses still share one source of error? | Compare viewpoints, communication and independence instead of counting reports alone. |
+
+## 02. Optical and sensor interpretation
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-017 | How can parallax make an object appear to move unusually fast? | Model observer motion, distance uncertainty and background references using a clearly illustrative geometry. |
+| BANK-033-018 | What can an infrared image reveal without identifying the object's exact shape? | Explain resolution, heat patterns, optics, tracking and processing limits. |
+| BANK-033-019 | How do zoom, stabilization and camera rotation affect apparent aerial motion? | Trace metadata and reference features rather than treating the display frame as a fixed physical coordinate system. |
+| BANK-033-020 | Why can radar detection require corroboration before assigning an object identity? | Compare tracking, noise, geometry, classification and missing context at an explanatory level. |
+
+## 03. Witnesses and records
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-021 | How can time between observation and interview affect a sighting account? | Compare memory, suggestion, later media exposure and independently recorded details. |
+| BANK-033-022 | What distinguishes independent corroboration from repeated publication of one report? | Trace source chains, timestamps and shared evidence rather than counting headlines. |
+| BANK-033-023 | How should a documentary treat an anonymous official source? | Explain verified access, corroboration, limitations and unresolved claims without equating anonymity with authority or falsehood. |
+| BANK-033-024 | What does declassification establish and leave unknown? | Separate publication status, omitted context, redaction and the evidence required for the underlying claim. |
+
+## 04. Historical UFO narratives
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-025 | How do famous sighting stories change as later details are added? | Compare contemporary records, later testimony and popular retellings in a bounded case. |
+| BANK-033-026 | What can a historical photograph establish without a reliable negative or original file? | Examine provenance, copies, context and tests possible on the surviving material. |
+| BANK-033-027 | How should a claim of a recovered object be investigated through documents? | Trace custody, physical access, independent examination and the difference between allegation and inspected evidence. |
+| BANK-033-028 | Why do unsupported cover-up explanations often become difficult to test? | Identify what evidence would count against the claim rather than treating every absence as confirmation. |
+
+## 05. Life beyond Earth
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-029 | Why is habitability different from evidence that a world is inhabited? | Compare environment, detection limits, unknown conditions and actual biological observations. |
+| BANK-033-030 | What can atmospheric chemistry suggest without proving life? | Inspect competing abiotic pathways, retrieval uncertainty and follow-up observations. |
+| BANK-033-031 | How can searches avoid assuming extraterrestrial organisms must resemble familiar animals? | Distinguish practical biomarkers, broader definitions and the limits of current instruments. |
+| BANK-033-032 | What does finding an extreme environment inhabited on Earth establish about other planets? | Separate demonstrated terrestrial adaptation from assumptions about origin and survival elsewhere. |
+
+## 06. Technosignatures
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-033 | What must a narrowband radio candidate survive before being treated as extraordinary evidence? | Compare interference, instrument effects, repeat observations and independent confirmation. |
+| BANK-033-034 | How can an apparent technological pattern emerge from natural processes or data selection? | State search methods, trial counts and alternative explanations rather than relying on pattern recognition alone. |
+| BANK-033-035 | Why does a non-detection constrain only particular searches? | Specify sky coverage, time, sensitivity, frequencies and assumed signal types. |
+| BANK-033-036 | How can the Drake equation organize uncertainty without predicting an exact civilization count? | Explain each assumption and sensitivity instead of presenting speculative inputs as measured values. |
+
+## 07. Institutions and communication
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-037 | What can an official investigation's mandate limit it from concluding? | Compare assigned questions, access, data quality and actual findings using the published report. |
+| BANK-033-038 | How should a channel distinguish testimony at a hearing from verified investigative conclusions? | Identify the procedural setting, evidence presented and unresolved verification. |
+| BANK-033-039 | What would responsible public communication of a possible extraterrestrial detection require? | Prioritize independent checks, uncertainty and accurate scope rather than a premature declaration. |
+| BANK-033-040 | How can national-security secrecy limit analysis without supporting every extraordinary claim? | State the specific missing information and avoid converting uncertainty into proof. |
+
+## 08. Documentary standards
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-033-041 | How can a visual reconstruction clarify a sighting without fabricating apparent evidence? | Label modeled geometry and assumed parameters rather than imitating undisclosed original footage. |
+| BANK-033-042 | What makes a title about aliens stronger than the evidence in the episode? | Compare its implied conclusion with the actual observation, alternatives and uncertainty. |
+| BANK-033-043 | How should a video be corrected after an object receives a credible identification? | Update the central claim and retained promotional imagery, citing the new evidence and its limits. |
+| BANK-033-044 | How can a documentary preserve curiosity without treating every explanation as equally supported? | Compare testable predictions, data access and strength of evidence rather than balancing conclusions for entertainment. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
