+# 054 Consciousness & Philosophy: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Consciousness & Philosophy. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Questions and conceptual boundaries
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-013 | What do philosophers mean by consciousness in different debates? | Separate wakefulness, subjective experience, access and self-awareness before comparing theories. |
+| BANK-054-014 | Why is explaining behavior different from explaining subjective experience? | Present the distinction and competing responses without assuming the explanatory gap settles the debate. |
+| BANK-054-015 | How can a thought experiment clarify a question without proving its premises true? | Identify the imagined conditions, intuition being tested and objections in one consciousness debate. |
+| BANK-054-016 | What makes a philosophical argument valid rather than merely persuasive? | Compare premises, inference and soundness using explicitly constructed examples without relying on rhetorical confidence. |
+
+## 02. Mind and body positions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-017 | What distinguishes physicalism, dualism and idealism about mind? | Compare their central commitments and internal varieties without reducing each position to a caricature. |
+| BANK-054-018 | How do identity theories differ from functional accounts of mental states? | Explain the role of physical realization and causal organization with bounded examples and objections. |
+| BANK-054-019 | What does panpsychism propose and what explanatory problems does it face? | Distinguish minimal experiential claims from attributing human thought to every object and include the combination problem. |
+| BANK-054-020 | How do emergentist accounts explain the relationship between parts and experience? | Compare weaker and stronger emergence claims while labeling contested explanatory commitments. |
+
+## 03. Scientific approaches to consciousness
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-021 | What can neural correlates of consciousness establish? | Separate association, enabling conditions and causal explanation through primary research examples chosen during source verification. |
+| BANK-054-022 | How do report-based and no-report experiments face different limitations? | Compare measurement, attention, inference and the difficulty of establishing experience independently. |
+| BANK-054-023 | Why do sleep and anesthesia studies challenge a simple on-off model of consciousness? | Frame states and measures through current research needs without offering diagnosis or clinical guidance. |
+| BANK-054-024 | How can competing consciousness theories be tested without assuming one theory's preferred measure? | Compare predictions, experimental design and interpretation criteria while leaving verdicts pending evidence review. |
+
+## 04. Self, identity and memory
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-025 | What makes personal identity over time different from momentary self-awareness? | Compare continuity of body, memory and psychological relations through explicit philosophical positions. |
+| BANK-054-026 | How do memory gaps challenge a simple autobiographical account of the self? | Discuss conceptual implications and research boundaries without diagnosing individuals or equating memory loss with loss of personhood. |
+| BANK-054-027 | What does the split-brain literature contribute to philosophical questions about unity? | Separate documented task results, interpretation and stronger claims about multiple selves pending primary-source review. |
+| BANK-054-028 | How do narrative accounts of identity handle social relationships? | Compare self-description, recognition and changing life stories without implying identity is freely invented without constraints. |
+
+## 05. Indian philosophical traditions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Identify the text, edition, translator, commentary, community and ritual context as applicable. Attribute theological and spiritual claims, preserve regional variation and respect public versus restricted knowledge.
+
+**Source types to locate:** primary texts in traceable editions; authorized public teaching and ritual descriptions; consented community accounts and critical historical studies. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-029 | How do Advaita accounts distinguish consciousness from changing mental contents? | Use identified texts and commentarial positions while distinguishing philosophical exposition from empirical proof. |
+| BANK-054-030 | How do Buddhist no-self arguments differ across schools? | Compare a bounded set of traditions and sources without presenting all Buddhist thought as one doctrine. |
+| BANK-054-031 | What do Samkhya and Yoga traditions claim about purusha and mental activity? | Explain their conceptual vocabulary and textual setting without translating every term directly into modern neuroscience. |
+| BANK-054-032 | How do Nyaya philosophers argue for a knowing subject? | Present a specific argument, objections and source context rather than treating a historical school as unanimous across centuries. |
+
+## 06. Knowledge, perception and agency
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-033 | What does an illusion reveal about perception without proving that all experience is false? | Compare appearance, interpretation and external-world claims through clearly bounded examples. |
+| BANK-054-034 | How do compatibilist and incompatibilist accounts frame free will differently? | Define the freedom at issue and compare arguments without using a single experiment as a final verdict. |
+| BANK-054-035 | Why does disagreement about evidence not automatically imply that all beliefs are equally justified? | Separate fallibility, standards of justification and relativist claims in a concise argument comparison. |
+| BANK-054-036 | What can phenomenology contribute that third-person measurement does not directly describe? | Explain first-person methods, aims and limitations without treating introspection as infallible evidence. |
+
+## 07. Other minds and artificial systems
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-037 | What justifies attributing experience to another being? | Compare behavior, biological similarity, inference and philosophical objections without pretending certainty is equally available in every case. |
+| BANK-054-038 | How should animal consciousness discussions distinguish kinds of evidence? | Separate behavioral flexibility, neurobiology and theoretical assumptions without ranking species on an unsupported single ladder. |
+| BANK-054-039 | What would a claim that an AI system is conscious need to specify? | Define the proposed capacity, theory-dependent indicators, alternatives and unresolved inference rather than equating fluent output with experience. |
+| BANK-054-040 | Why does simulating a mental process raise different questions from having an experience? | Compare computational explanation, implementation and philosophical positions without declaring the debate settled. |
+
+## 08. Ethics and responsible interpretation
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-054-041 | How does uncertainty about consciousness affect moral consideration? | Compare precaution, graded evidence and competing ethical approaches without presenting one policy as logically mandatory. |
+| BANK-054-042 | What can clinical consciousness assessments teach philosophers about measurement limits? | Describe the distinction between observable response and inferred awareness through authoritative research, with no patient-specific advice. |
+| BANK-054-043 | How should extraordinary claims about consciousness be evaluated? | Separate reproducible observations, interpretation, anecdote and claims that currently lack testable predictions. |
+| BANK-054-044 | How can a documentary present unresolved consciousness questions without manufacturing false balance? | Identify established observations, live scholarly disagreements and unsupported assertions at different evidential levels. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
