+## 06. Philosophical accounts of temporal reality
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-055-033 | What distinguishes presentism from eternalism? | Compare what each position claims exists and how proponents respond to relativity without assigning a settled philosophical winner. |
+| BANK-055-034 | Does the passage of time require more than change? | Present competing accounts, their conceptual motivations and objections with ordinary-language examples. |
+| BANK-055-035 | How do A-theory and B-theory frame temporal facts differently? | Explain tense, ordering and disputed claims about objective becoming rather than equating terminology with rival physical equations. |
+| BANK-055-036 | What does a relationist account of time claim compared with substantivalism? | Compare the dependence of time on events and the historical arguments without treating old positions as modern scientific results. |
+
+## 07. Time travel and causal puzzles
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Declare a conditional scenario, not a prediction. Anchor present-day capabilities in evidence, make physical and institutional assumptions explicit, and trace second-order consequences and failure conditions.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current original research on the enabling technologies; physical and economic constraints with explicit inputs; published scenario methods and relevant legal frameworks. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-055-037 | What makes travel into the future different from returning to one's own past? | Separate differential aging supported by relativity from speculative causal structures and fictional devices. |
+| BANK-055-038 | How do consistency approaches handle a grandfather-style paradox? | Explain the assumptions of the thought experiment and proposed resolutions without claiming past-directed travel has been demonstrated. |
+| BANK-055-039 | What are closed timelike curves in a theoretical spacetime model? | Distinguish mathematical solutions, physical feasibility and unresolved constraints at a conceptual level. |
+| BANK-055-040 | Why do branching-timeline stories not automatically follow from quantum theory? | Compare fictional rules with carefully stated interpretations and avoid treating an entertainment convention as an experimental result. |
