+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-055-041 | Why can felt duration differ from clock duration? | Use psychological research on attention and memory with context and limits, avoiding medical interpretation of personal symptoms. |
+| BANK-055-042 | How should a documentary evaluate claims that reality is a simulation? | Separate philosophical possibility, proposed tests and unsupported assertions while stating what evidence would distinguish hypotheses. |
+| BANK-055-043 | What makes an animation of curved spacetime helpful and potentially misleading? | Identify the analogy's scope and the features it cannot represent instead of letting a rubber-sheet image serve as proof. |
+| BANK-055-044 | How can a time-and-reality series mark the boundary between established physics and speculation? | Use recurring labels for measured result, model implication, interpretation and fictional extrapolation. |
