+# 063 Consumer Technology: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 31 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Consumer Technology. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Understanding connected products
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-013 | How does a smart device depend on a companion app and a cloud account? | Map setup, local controls, remote services and failure modes for a documented product; identify which functions require internet access without assuming all devices work alike. |
+| BANK-063-014 | What does a product specification omit about daily usability? | Compare an actual task sequence, accessibility, setup time and recovery from errors; separate stated features from conditions observed in a reproducible trial. |
+| BANK-063-015 | Why can two phones with similar camera specifications produce different results? | Compare optics, processing, exposure and a controlled scene set; distinguish subjective preference from measurable artifacts and avoid megapixel-only rankings. |
+| BANK-063-016 | How can product-generation names obscure meaningful hardware differences? | Resolve exact regional model numbers, chipsets and supported bands from official records; treat retailer shorthand as a lead requiring confirmation. |
+
+## 02. Displays, audio and capture
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-017 | What does display brightness mean under different measurement conditions? | Separate peak-window, full-screen and sustained output with test conditions; include ambient light and readability without comparing incompatible advertised numbers. |
+| BANK-063-018 | How can headphone noise cancellation be tested without confusing it with isolation? | Compare powered and unpowered behavior, fit and frequency-dependent attenuation; use safe playback levels and avoid medical claims about hearing protection. |
+| BANK-063-019 | What changes between optical zoom, sensor cropping and software enlargement? | Follow a fixed subject through documented capture modes; inspect detail and artifacts rather than accepting every zoom multiplier as equivalent. |
+| BANK-063-020 | Why can a video call sound poor even with a good microphone? | Trace room acoustics, placement, codec, network and processing settings; use permission-cleared recordings and distinguish capture problems from transmission problems. |
+
+## 03. Batteries and charging
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-021 | How should battery-life tests account for the way a device is used? | Specify brightness, radios, applications, temperature and standby time; distinguish repeated controlled tests from an all-day marketing claim. |
+| BANK-063-022 | Why can a charger with a larger wattage label charge a device at the same speed? | Inspect negotiated profiles, device limits, cable support and charge-stage behavior; exclude improvised adapters and rely on official compatibility data. |
+| BANK-063-023 | What does a battery-health percentage reveal and leave uncertain? | Review manufacturer estimation methods, cycle definitions and service guidance; separate estimated capacity from a complete safety or runtime diagnosis. |
+
+## 04. Home devices and interoperability
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-024 | How can a smart-home purchase be evaluated for operation during an internet outage? | Test permitted local commands, automations and account dependencies in an owned setup; record firmware and distinguish router failure from cloud failure. |
+| BANK-063-025 | What does a shared interoperability standard guarantee for a smart-home device? | Compare certified functions, controller requirements and vendor extensions using current specifications; do not equate a logo with identical feature support. |
+| BANK-063-026 | How should a household compare robot-vacuum results across different floors? | Define debris, thresholds, rugs, obstacles and maintenance state; keep mapping privacy and replacement parts in scope rather than relying on a single cleaning score. |
+| BANK-063-027 | Why can adding a smart camera create privacy obligations for other people? | Map capture area, recording, account access and deletion controls; use official rules for the jurisdiction and obtain consent for any demonstration involving identifiable people. |
+
+## 05. Privacy, accounts and recurring costs
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-028 | What remains usable when a connected product's subscription is cancelled? | Inspect dated terms, local storage, exports and basic controls for the exact plan; distinguish confirmed retained features from assumptions about future policy. |
+| BANK-063-029 | How can a device's privacy notice be connected to its actual settings? | Map data categories, defaults, optional telemetry and deletion paths; do not claim an interface test proves all backend behavior. |
+| BANK-063-030 | What should a family verify before giving a connected device to a child? | Review age rules, parental controls, purchases, contacts and data handling from official sources; evaluate setup tradeoffs without claiming any setting eliminates risk. |
+| BANK-063-031 | How do app-store permissions differ from access granted inside a product account? | Compare operating-system permissions, OAuth scopes and shared-account roles with a bounded example; avoid conflating denial of one permission with complete data isolation. |
+
+## 06. Support, repair and ownership
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-032 | How does an advertised support period translate into usable device life? | Separate security updates, feature updates, repairs and cloud-service availability; verify the exact model's dated commitment and exceptions. |
+| BANK-063-033 | What can a teardown reveal that a repairability score may hide? | Compare fasteners, adhesives, calibration, parts pairing and manuals using authorized documentation; exclude hazardous disassembly instructions. |
+| BANK-063-034 | How should a device trade-in be assessed beyond its quoted value? | Examine eligibility, inspection adjustments, transfer of accounts and return terms; require current local terms rather than treating a quote as a guaranteed payout. |
+| BANK-063-035 | What happens when a company shuts down the service behind a product? | Trace documented announcements, export windows, replacement functions and consumer remedies in one case; avoid assuming all owners had identical outcomes. |
+
+## 07. Reviews, marketing and measurement
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-036 | How can sponsored technology content disclose its evidence and commercial relationships? | Separate product access, payment, affiliate incentives and editorial method; inspect applicable disclosure rules and do not infer dishonesty solely from sponsorship. |
+| BANK-063-037 | Why can a benchmark lead to a different conclusion from a long-term usability review? | Compare controlled measurements, sample variation, software changes and lived tasks; define the question each review method can actually answer. |
+| BANK-063-038 | How should an AI feature demonstration be checked for hidden assistance? | Examine workflow boundaries, connectivity, human intervention and edited footage using original test material; avoid asserting undisclosed manipulation without evidence. |
+| BANK-063-039 | What makes a comparison fair when one device has received a major update? | Record firmware, settings, reset conditions and retest dates for both products; distinguish launch performance from current observed behavior. |
+
+## 08. Accessibility, sustainability and emerging categories
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-063-040 | When can a wearable's wellness number be mistaken for a clinical measurement? | Compare the manufacturer's intended use, validation population and known limitations; leave diagnosis and treatment outside a consumer feature review. |
+| BANK-063-041 | How can an accessibility feature be evaluated with the people expected to use it? | Define a consented task study, assistive settings and failure reporting; include individual differences instead of treating one reviewer as representative. |
+| BANK-063-042 | What evidence is needed to assess a product's environmental claim? | Specify lifecycle boundary, repair life, energy, materials and independent disclosures; separate measured reductions from offsets and unsupported green language. |
+| BANK-063-043 | How can a new gadget category be evaluated before a stable benchmark exists? | Define useful tasks, baseline alternatives, constraints and reproducible observations; label judgments and avoid presenting early prototypes as mature products. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
