+# 070 Career & Jobs: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 33 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Career & Jobs. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Mapping occupations and requirements
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-013 | How can someone distinguish a job title from the work actually performed? | Compare consented worker accounts, official occupational descriptions and real role tasks; separate employer-specific duties from assumptions attached to a fashionable title. |
+| BANK-070-014 | What does a job advertisement reveal and omit about an ordinary workday? | Inspect responsibilities, reporting lines, schedule, performance measures and missing information across dated public ads; avoid inferring workplace culture from slogans alone. |
+| BANK-070-015 | How can an occupational profile separate entry routes from the paths of already successful workers? | Compare formal requirements, apprenticeships, portfolios and career histories with selection bias explicit; do not present one prominent person's route as typical. |
+| BANK-070-016 | Why should career exploration include undesirable tasks as well as attractive outcomes? | Map repetitive work, constraints, customer contact and responsibility through multiple consented accounts; avoid treating prestige or salary as a complete fit assessment. |
+
+## 02. Skills, learning and credentials
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-017 | How can a skill gap be identified from actual job tasks rather than a long course catalogue? | Translate a bounded role into demonstrable tasks, prerequisite knowledge and evidence; distinguish mandatory requirements from preferences in current official role information. |
+| BANK-070-018 | What makes a portfolio item useful evidence of a candidate's contribution? | Show problem, constraints, personal work, results and rights-cleared artifacts in an original example; disclose team contributions and exclude confidential employer material. |
+| BANK-070-019 | When does a credential represent a legal requirement rather than a hiring preference? | Consult the regulator, awarding body and employer requirements for a named occupation and jurisdiction; avoid assuming international recognition or permanent validity. |
+| BANK-070-020 | How can an apprenticeship be compared with a classroom-only training route? | Inspect supervised work, assessment, wages or fees, recognized outcomes and completion evidence; verify dated official terms rather than guaranteeing employment. |
+
+## 03. Search strategy and applications
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-021 | How can a resume make achievements assessable without inventing numerical impact? | Revise an original example to state work, context and attributable outcomes; keep estimates labeled and avoid copying fabricated accomplishments into an application. |
+| BANK-070-022 | What changes when an application must be readable by both people and software? | Compare clear headings, accessible text and faithful role keywords with official submission requirements; exclude keyword stuffing and promises of beating every screening system. |
+| BANK-070-023 | How can a cover letter explain a career transition with evidence? | Connect transferable tasks, relevant learning and a specific role using an invented candidate; avoid generic passion statements or concealing missing mandatory qualifications. |
+| BANK-070-024 | What can a job-search record reveal beyond the number of applications sent? | Track role fit, referral source, stage, feedback and follow-up with privacy controls; avoid treating response rates from a small sample as a verdict on personal worth. |
+
+## 04. Interviews and hiring decisions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-025 | How can a candidate prepare examples that answer a behavioral interview question clearly? | Use an original situation-action-result account with contribution and limitations explicit; avoid scripting invented experiences or implying one answer guarantees selection. |
+| BANK-070-026 | What should be clarified before agreeing to an unpaid hiring assignment? | Examine scope, time, ownership, confidentiality and the employer's stated purpose; verify current local rules and avoid giving a universal legal judgment. |
+| BANK-070-027 | How can a technical interview be analyzed separately from competence on the job? | Compare assessed tasks, time pressure, scoring and role relevance using published or consented examples; avoid inferring all hiring validity from a personal anecdote. |
+| BANK-070-028 | What questions help reveal how success in a role is actually evaluated? | Investigate priorities, support, decision authority and review practices in an illustrative interview; distinguish an employer's promise from evidence of implementation. |
+
+## 05. Offers, work arrangements and rights
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-029 | What should be compared in two job offers beyond headline salary? | Map base pay, variable pay, hours, leave, benefits, location and conditions using dated documents and illustrative figures; leave personal tax or legal conclusions to qualified local guidance. |
+| BANK-070-030 | How can remote-work terms differ from the impression given by a job advertisement? | Inspect location restrictions, equipment, monitoring, hours and written attendance rules; use current official terms and avoid assuming a permanent entitlement from informal language. |
+| BANK-070-031 | What distinguishes an employee, contractor and platform worker in a career-planning episode? | Consult official tests and protections for a named jurisdiction; separate contract wording, actual working arrangements and disputed classification without deciding an individual's status. |
+| BANK-070-032 | How can a worker verify the terms of probation before accepting a role? | Check the written offer, official employment rules, notice and evaluation arrangements; do not assume the label removes all rights or means the same thing everywhere. |
+
+## 06. Starting work and professional development
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-033 | What can a new employee clarify during the first month to reduce avoidable confusion? | Map priorities, decision makers, communication practices, training and feedback through an original onboarding plan; avoid equating constant availability with professionalism. |
+| BANK-070-034 | How can a person request useful feedback when a performance review is vague? | Develop concrete questions around examples, expected behavior and support; use consented or fictional exchanges and do not infer unfair intent from limited information. |
+| BANK-070-035 | What separates a promotion in title from a change in scope and authority? | Compare decision rights, accountability, compensation and resources in a documented or invented role transition; keep employer-specific policies distinct from universal career rules. |
+| BANK-070-036 | How can mentoring relationships be designed around a bounded learning need? | Define goals, time, confidentiality and feedback with both participants' consent; distinguish mentorship from sponsorship, therapy or guaranteed access to opportunities. |
+
+## 07. Transitions, breaks and labor markets
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-037 | How can a career-change budget make uncertainty visible before resignation? | Use transparent illustrative costs, runway, training time and income scenarios; avoid return promises or individualized financial recommendations. |
+| BANK-070-038 | What evidence helps assess whether an occupation's reported growth translates into accessible jobs? | Compare official projections, openings, region, entry barriers and experience requirements; distinguish forecasts from vacancies currently available to a particular candidate. |
+| BANK-070-039 | How can a career break be explained without disclosing private health or family details? | Develop honest role-relevant examples of readiness and retained skills; check local rights and avoid implying an applicant must reveal sensitive circumstances. |
+| BANK-070-040 | Why can automation forecasts tell different stories about the same occupation? | Compare task-based measures, adoption assumptions, time horizons and official labor data; separate technical capability from job-loss predictions. |
+| BANK-070-041 | How should a redundancy or layoff episode distinguish an announcement from workers' actual outcomes? | Trace official notices, timelines, support and consented accounts for a defined case; avoid rumors and do not infer an individual's prospects from company headlines. |
+
+## 08. Access, integrity and long-term choices
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-070-042 | How can a job seeker evaluate a suspicious recruitment approach? | Inspect employer identity, official application channels, requested payments and data demands using authority guidance; exclude interacting with suspected scammers or publishing unverified allegations. |
+| BANK-070-043 | What should a worker verify before sharing personal information in a background-check process? | Review legitimate provider identity, consent, purpose, required data and local rules; avoid collecting real identifying documents for a demonstration. |
+| BANK-070-044 | How can workplace accessibility be investigated before an application becomes an individual accommodation dispute? | Compare published facilities, task requirements, official procedures and consented worker experiences; do not decide eligibility or assume a disability implies particular limitations. |
+| BANK-070-045 | What makes a career decision reversible or costly to reverse? | Compare credential portability, relocation, debt, networks and re-entry options through explicit scenarios; distinguish personal values from claims about an objectively best career. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
