+# 071 Productivity & Self-Improvement: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 31 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Productivity & Self-Improvement. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Goals, priorities and realistic capacity
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-013 | How can a person distinguish a chosen goal from an obligation inherited from other people? | Use an original reflective planning example to separate preferences, duties and external pressure; avoid diagnosing motives or asserting one correct definition of success. |
+| BANK-071-014 | What makes a weekly plan feasible when paid work and care responsibilities compete? | Map fixed commitments, transition time, variable demands and rest using an illustrative calendar; distinguish a capacity estimate from a moral measure of effort. |
+| BANK-071-015 | How can a large ambition become a next action that actually reduces uncertainty? | Turn an invented learning project into a question, a small deliverable and a review point; avoid assuming that breaking work into more tasks always clarifies it. |
+| BANK-071-016 | Why can prioritization fail even when every task has an urgency label? | Compare deadlines, consequences, dependencies and decision authority; use a bounded work scenario rather than treating one matrix as a universal planning solution. |
+
+## 02. Attention and digital environments
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-017 | What does task switching cost in a particular kind of work? | Inspect original studies for task similarity, interruptions, accuracy and timing; distinguish laboratory effects from a fixed productivity-loss percentage for everyone. |
+| BANK-071-018 | How can notification settings be evaluated against actual communication needs? | Design a voluntary before-and-after observation of interruptions, missed messages and perceived control; record the device settings and avoid assuming fewer alerts always helps. |
+| BANK-071-019 | Why can an unfinished task remain mentally intrusive after the workday ends? | Compare proposed mechanisms, original experiments and limits of generalization; separate an attention phenomenon from a diagnosis of anxiety or a promise of relief. |
+| BANK-071-020 | When can background sound support one task while interfering with another? | Review task demands, language content, volume and participant variation; avoid claiming that a frequency, playlist or genre universally improves cognition. |
+
+## 03. Habits and environment design
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-021 | How can a habit be distinguished from a behavior sustained by repeated deliberate effort? | Define cues, context stability and measures of automaticity from original research; exclude a universal number of days for habit formation. |
+| BANK-071-022 | What does changing the environment alter in a habit-building plan? | Compare friction, visibility and timing for one harmless routine; separate plausible design principles from demonstrated long-term adherence. |
+| BANK-071-023 | Why can a routine disappear after a move or schedule change? | Investigate context cues, competing demands and maintenance evidence; use an illustrative case without equating disruption with weak character. |
+| BANK-071-024 | How can a lapse be recorded without turning it into an all-or-nothing judgment? | Compare behavior logs, context and adjustment options in a voluntary routine; avoid presenting journaling as treatment or a guarantee against recurrence. |
+
+## 04. Procrastination, motivation and emotions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-025 | What different problems can be hidden behind the word procrastination? | Compare task ambiguity, aversion, competing demands and research definitions; distinguish an educational analysis from diagnosing an individual's mental health. |
+| BANK-071-026 | How can an implementation intention be evaluated beyond writing an if-then sentence? | Inspect original studies, specified cues, feasible responses and actual follow-through; avoid implying a plan removes structural barriers or clinical symptoms. |
+| BANK-071-027 | Why can a reward change the meaning of a task as well as its completion rate? | Review intrinsic motivation, incentive conditions and measured outcomes in named experiments; do not reduce all incentives to either helpful or harmful. |
+| BANK-071-028 | What should be questioned before calling a person unmotivated? | Consider resources, unclear expectations, health constraints and task fit through consented accounts; avoid remote diagnosis or treating productivity advice as adequate support for illness. |
+
+## 05. Planning systems and information tools
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-029 | When does a task manager become another place where work is lost? | Trace capture, clarification, review and retrieval in an original workflow; compare actual failure points rather than ranking applications from feature lists. |
+| BANK-071-030 | How should calendar blocking account for work whose duration is uncertain? | Use ranges, buffers and review points in an illustrative project; distinguish estimated capacity from guaranteed output and disclose invented timings. |
+| BANK-071-031 | What makes a note useful when it is revisited months later? | Compare source attribution, context, retrieval cues and links in original notes; avoid equating elaborate categorization with understanding or memory. |
+| BANK-071-032 | How can automation reduce a repetitive task without hiding new errors? | Choose a reversible local workflow with input checks, exceptions and a visible audit; exclude unauthorized account actions and measure review work as part of cost. |
+
+## 06. Learning, creativity and reflective practice
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-033 | How can deliberate practice be separated from simply repeating an activity? | Inspect defined skills, feedback, challenge and study populations in original research; avoid promising expertise after a fixed number of hours. |
+| BANK-071-034 | What does a review of completed work reveal that a streak counter does not? | Compare quality, retained learning, obstacles and changed priorities through an invented project record; distinguish output quantity from skill growth. |
+| BANK-071-035 | How can a creative project reserve space for exploration without losing delivery constraints? | Map divergent drafts, selection criteria and deadlines using a permission-cleared example; keep creative judgment separate from unsupported neuroscience claims. |
+| BANK-071-036 | Why can comparing a beginner's process with an expert's finished output distort self-assessment? | Contrast drafts, revisions, support and selection effects through documented work histories; avoid inferring the expert's private effort or mental state. |
+
+## 07. Rest, limits and unequal conditions
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Inspect current professional guidance and original studies for the exact population, intervention or measurement. Report comparators, absolute outcomes, uncertainty, harms and limits. Do not diagnose, prescribe or imply that education replaces professional care.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current official clinical or public-health guidance; original trials, cohort studies or diagnostic-validation reports; study registrations, protocols and adverse-event records. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-037 | How should a productivity episode discuss sleep without converting research into a personal treatment plan? | Use current health guidance and original studies on cognition, population and sleep conditions; exclude individualized sleep prescriptions or claims that a routine cures fatigue. |
+| BANK-071-038 | When does workplace exhaustion require a discussion of job conditions rather than a new personal system? | Compare demands, control, staffing and support using official occupational-health definitions; avoid diagnosing burnout or claiming self-optimization resolves organizational harm. |
+| BANK-071-039 | How can productivity methods be adapted with people who have fluctuating energy? | Use consented preferences, flexible commitments and access needs; distinguish accommodation ideas from clinical advice or assumptions about a diagnosis. |
+| BANK-071-040 | What does a time-use diary reveal about unequal access to uninterrupted work? | Compare caregiving, paid hours, commute and household labor through official data and consented examples; do not treat time use as a universal personal choice. |
+
+## 08. Claims, values and long-term experiments
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-071-041 | How can a self-improvement experiment avoid mistaking novelty for lasting change? | Specify a baseline, follow-up, comparable conditions and unintended costs; label self-observation limits and avoid generalizing one person's result. |
+| BANK-071-042 | What evidence supports a productivity method besides a creator's success story? | Compare original evaluations, selection effects, conflicts of interest and the exact promised outcome; separate testimonial value from causal proof. |
+| BANK-071-043 | When should a goal be revised instead of pursued more efficiently? | Examine changed constraints, opportunity costs, values and evidence of usefulness through a bounded scenario; avoid prescribing when any real person should abandon a commitment. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
