+# 072 Relationships: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 31 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Relationships. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Understanding relationship context
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-013 | How can two people describe the same relationship differently without one account explaining everything? | Compare expectations, roles and specific interactions through fictional examples; avoid diagnosing a real person or assuming intent from one narrative. |
+| BANK-072-014 | What changes when relationship expectations are discussed explicitly rather than assumed? | Explore time together, privacy, money and responsibilities using original dialogue; distinguish negotiation from a guarantee of agreement or safety. |
+| BANK-072-015 | How do friendships, family ties and romantic partnerships create different obligations? | Use attributed cultural and individual perspectives; avoid making one household or relationship structure the universal standard. |
+
+## 02. Communication and listening
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-016 | How can a listener check their understanding without turning a conversation into a scripted exercise? | Compare paraphrase, specific questions and correction in an invented exchange; preserve both participants' agency and avoid promising that a technique resolves every conflict. |
+| BANK-072-017 | Why can the timing of a difficult discussion matter as much as its wording? | Examine privacy, fatigue, urgency and willingness to participate; exclude advice to delay urgent safety needs or force another person into a conversation. |
+| BANK-072-018 | What makes a request clearer than an accusation about someone's character? | Compare observable events, impact and a bounded requested change in fictional dialogue; avoid suggesting wording alone makes coercive behavior safe. |
+| BANK-072-019 | How can written messages lose context that would be available in conversation? | Analyze tone, delay, ambiguity and repair using invented texts; avoid presenting response speed or punctuation as reliable evidence of affection or deception. |
+
+## 03. Boundaries, consent and autonomy
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-020 | What distinguishes a personal boundary from an attempt to control another adult? | Compare statements about one's participation with imposed surveillance or restrictions using fictional cases; consult qualified sources and do not adjudicate a real dispute. |
+| BANK-072-021 | How can consent be discussed as an ongoing process rather than a one-time assumption? | Use authoritative public education resources on freely given participation, change and communication; keep legal definitions specific to jurisdiction and exclude explicit scenarios. |
+| BANK-072-022 | Why can access to a partner's phone become a privacy question rather than proof of trust? | Map voluntary sharing, pressure, account security and autonomy; avoid encouraging surveillance or treating either refusal or access as proof of infidelity. |
+| BANK-072-023 | How can someone decline a social request while preserving room for the relationship to continue? | Develop original examples around time, energy and commitments; distinguish respectful communication from a promise that the other person will accept the decision. |
+
+## 04. Conflict, repair and accountability
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-024 | What does relationship research actually measure when studying conflict patterns? | Review observation methods, participant samples, coding and follow-up in original studies; avoid assigning predictive scores to viewers or treating one clip as diagnostic. |
+| BANK-072-025 | How can an apology acknowledge harm without deciding that forgiveness is owed? | Compare specific responsibility, repair and changed behavior in fictional cases; preserve the affected person's choice and avoid guarantees of reconciliation. |
+| BANK-072-026 | When can a pause in an argument support a later conversation rather than become withdrawal? | Examine agreed timing, follow-up and safety context using qualified educational sources; do not prescribe return to an unsafe interaction. |
+| BANK-072-027 | Why can solving the practical dispute leave the emotional disagreement unresolved? | Separate the immediate decision, differing meanings and ongoing responsibilities in an original example; avoid reducing every conflict to a hidden psychological cause. |
+
+## 05. Friends, family and social change
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-028 | How do adult friendships change when work, distance and caregiving reduce shared time? | Use consented accounts from different circumstances to compare contact, reciprocity and expectations; avoid treating frequency as a universal closeness measure. |
+| BANK-072-029 | What can be negotiated when extended family expectations conflict with a couple's plans? | Explore visits, ceremonies, care and resources through attributed perspectives; avoid stereotyping a culture or prescribing estrangement as a default. |
+| BANK-072-030 | How can siblings discuss unequal caregiving responsibilities without erasing unequal resources? | Map paid work, proximity, money and care tasks through a fictional family; distinguish an arrangement's appearance from each person's actual capacity. |
+| BANK-072-031 | Why can grief change communication within a household in different ways? | Use recognized bereavement education and consented accounts; exclude fixed stages, recovery deadlines or diagnosing anyone's response. |
+
+## 06. Money, domestic work and major transitions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-032 | What should a couple clarify before combining household expenses? | Map access, contributions, debt disclosure, emergencies and decision rules using illustrative budgets; verify local legal and financial consequences before scripting advice. |
+| BANK-072-033 | How can unequal income affect negotiating power without determining the whole relationship? | Compare account access, unpaid work and decision authority through consented accounts; avoid declaring equality from equal payments or assuming exploitation from income differences alone. |
+| BANK-072-034 | What changes in a relationship when one person becomes a caregiver? | Investigate shifting roles, support, privacy and rest using ethical accounts and qualified care resources; avoid prescribing care arrangements or assuming affection removes strain. |
+| BANK-072-035 | How can a relocation decision include the opportunities each person might lose? | Compare employment, support networks, access needs and reversibility in an explicit scenario; distinguish shared decision making from an objective calculation of whose needs matter more. |
+
+## 07. Evidence and harmful patterns
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Inspect current professional guidance and original studies for the exact population, intervention or measurement. Report comparators, absolute outcomes, uncertainty, harms and limits. Do not diagnose, prescribe or imply that education replaces professional care.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current official clinical or public-health guidance; original trials, cohort studies or diagnostic-validation reports; study registrations, protocols and adverse-event records. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-036 | How can a relationship episode describe coercive control without diagnosing a personality disorder? | Use current official public-health or safeguarding definitions and documented behavior categories; avoid labels based on armchair analysis or encouraging confrontation. |
+| BANK-072-037 | Why should advice for ordinary disagreement not be copied into a threatening relationship? | Contrast voluntary negotiation with power, fear and safety constraints using authoritative support guidance; exclude mediation scripts or actions that could increase immediate danger. |
+| BANK-072-038 | What limits the usefulness of online attachment-style quizzes? | Inspect the underlying construct, validation, self-report bias and intended use; distinguish an educational framework from a diagnosis or permanent identity. |
+| BANK-072-039 | How can claims about gender differences in relationships be evaluated fairly? | Compare study samples, cultural context, distributions and within-group variation; reject claims about an individual's behavior based on group averages. |
+
+## 08. Support, endings and ethical storytelling
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-072-040 | What can someone verify before choosing a relationship counselor or support service? | Examine credentials, scope, confidentiality, access and current local regulation; avoid recommending a service from testimonials alone or assuming joint sessions fit every situation. |
+| BANK-072-041 | How can a breakup discussion respect privacy without hiding relevant responsibilities? | Explore practical communication, shared commitments and agreed information boundaries using fictional cases; keep legal matters jurisdiction-specific and do not script pressure for reconciliation. |
+| BANK-072-042 | What does rebuilding a social network after a relationship ends require beyond advice to move on? | Use consented accounts of routines, community access, mutual friends and support; exclude fixed timelines or claims that a new partner is necessary for recovery. |
+| BANK-072-043 | How can a creator tell a relationship story without turning identifiable people into villains? | Plan informed consent, anonymization, right of reply where appropriate and fact-versus-interpretation labels; do not publish private messages or infer consent from prior posting. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
