+# 077 Yoga & Wellness: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 31 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Yoga & Wellness. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Scope of a yoga-and-wellness channel
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-013 | What belongs in a yoga wellness episode rather than a yoga-philosophy or posture-history lesson? | Define daily participation, service context and evidence appraisal as the primary scope; refer detailed textual study to bank 280 and breath protocols to bank 279. |
+| BANK-077-014 | How can a viewer distinguish a general yoga class from a claimed therapeutic service? | Compare stated aims, instructor scope, intake, assessment and evidence standards; verify local professional rules before discussing clinical roles. |
+| BANK-077-015 | Why does the word wellness need a specific outcome before it can be evaluated? | Separate enjoyment, function, stress measures and clinical endpoints using public programme descriptions; avoid treating a broad label as a measured benefit. |
+
+## 02. Joining a programme and informed choice
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-016 | What information can a newcomer request before attending a yoga class? | Map format, access, pace, equipment, touch policy and opportunities to pause; distinguish service information from personal medical clearance. |
+| BANK-077-017 | How can a class description communicate expected demands without promising suitability for everyone? | Compare floor access, transitions, balance demands and duration in original descriptions; avoid equating beginner labels with absence of risk. |
+| BANK-077-018 | What should be visible in an instructor's public qualifications and scope? | Check awarding bodies, training descriptions, insurance where relevant and local regulation; do not assume a certificate establishes clinical competence or universal teaching quality. |
+| BANK-077-019 | How can an introductory consultation respect privacy while identifying access needs? | Use minimal necessary questions, consent and clear referral boundaries; exclude collecting detailed health histories for a public content demonstration. |
+
+## 03. Everyday participation and learning
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-020 | How can a participant build a realistic attendance routine around irregular work? | Compare available sessions, travel time, home circumstances and flexibility through an illustrative schedule; avoid prescribing practice frequency or blaming missed attendance. |
+| BANK-077-021 | What does learning to pause or opt out change about participation in a class? | Explore explicit choices, teacher responses and consented participant experiences; distinguish supportive culture from evidence of a clinical intervention. |
+| BANK-077-022 | How can progress be discussed without treating deeper poses as the main goal? | Compare participant-defined aims, confidence, access and task observations; exclude diagnosing mobility or measuring worth through flexibility. |
+| BANK-077-023 | Why can online and in-person yoga classes require different expectations? | Examine feedback, visibility, privacy, space and emergency response arrangements; do not imply that a video teacher can assess every participant remotely. |
+
+## 04. Movement, adaptation and access
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect current professional guidance and original studies for the exact population, intervention or measurement. Report comparators, absolute outcomes, uncertainty, harms and limits. Do not diagnose, prescribe or imply that education replaces professional care.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current official clinical or public-health guidance; original trials, cohort studies or diagnostic-validation reports; study registrations, protocols and adverse-event records. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-024 | What questions should an accessible class answer about floor transfers and chair use? | Use qualified guidance and consented user requirements to inspect setup, options and assistance; avoid prescribing adaptations for an individual's diagnosis. |
+| BANK-077-025 | How can a yoga episode distinguish movement sensation from a medical explanation of pain? | Consult current clinical guidance and original pain research; keep participant descriptions separate from diagnosis and exclude instructions to push through symptoms. |
+| BANK-077-026 | Why can balance activities have different demands in different environments? | Compare support availability, vision, surface and transitions in a non-prescriptive analysis; leave individual fall-risk assessment to qualified professionals. |
+| BANK-077-027 | How should a teacher describe options for people with different body sizes? | Center consent, space, equipment and task access through varied participant accounts; avoid treating body size alone as evidence of ability or health. |
+
+## 05. Stress, rest and wellbeing evidence
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect current professional guidance and original studies for the exact population, intervention or measurement. Report comparators, absolute outcomes, uncertainty, harms and limits. Do not diagnose, prescribe or imply that education replaces professional care.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current official clinical or public-health guidance; original trials, cohort studies or diagnostic-validation reports; study registrations, protocols and adverse-event records. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-028 | What does a yoga trial mean by reduced stress? | Inspect the exact questionnaire, population, comparison, duration and absolute changes; distinguish self-report from clinical diagnosis and long-term outcomes. |
+| BANK-077-029 | How can a plausible relaxation mechanism be separated from proof that yoga treats an illness? | Compare mechanism studies with controlled clinical evidence for a defined outcome; exclude cure language or recommending replacement of established care. |
+| BANK-077-030 | What should be examined before claiming yoga improves sleep? | Review the studied programme, sleep measure, comparison, follow-up and harms; distinguish subjective sleep quality from diagnostic assessment or a universal sleep prescription. |
+| BANK-077-031 | Why do mindfulness, stretching and social contact complicate attribution in a yoga programme? | Map components, comparison groups and adherence in original trials; avoid assigning the entire outcome to a single preferred mechanism. |
+
+## 06. Specific populations and clinical boundaries
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Inspect current professional guidance and original studies for the exact population, intervention or measurement. Report comparators, absolute outcomes, uncertainty, harms and limits. Do not diagnose, prescribe or imply that education replaces professional care.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current official clinical or public-health guidance; original trials, cohort studies or diagnostic-validation reports; study registrations, protocols and adverse-event records. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-032 | How should yoga research involving older adults be evaluated for everyday applicability? | Compare eligibility, supervision, access, outcomes and adverse-event reporting; do not generalize from selected volunteers to every older person. |
+| BANK-077-033 | What should a pregnancy-related yoga episode verify before making a benefit or safety claim? | Use current professional guidance and original studies with gestational and clinical context explicit; exclude personalized sequences, clearance or assurances from limited trial data. |
+| BANK-077-034 | How can an episode discuss yoga in chronic-condition care without providing treatment? | Choose one defined condition and inspect current guidance, trial populations and adjunctive-care language; separate research questions from individualized recommendations. |
+| BANK-077-035 | Why is a trauma-sensitive service label not proof of clinical treatment competence? | Compare the stated approach, consent, staff training and referral scope using authoritative sources; avoid trauma diagnosis or eliciting public disclosures from participants. |
+
+## 07. Settings, community and commercial incentives
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-036 | How can a workplace yoga offer be evaluated without shifting responsibility for harmful work conditions onto staff? | Compare voluntary access, scheduling, confidentiality and organizational demands; distinguish participation satisfaction from evidence that structural stressors were resolved. |
+| BANK-077-037 | What changes when yoga is offered in a school or community center? | Examine consent, inclusion, religious interpretation, staff scope and accessibility under current local policy; avoid assuming every family has the same preference. |
+| BANK-077-038 | How should retreat marketing separate the programme from promises of personal transformation? | Inspect schedule, costs, instructor roles, access, cancellation terms and evidence for stated outcomes; do not infer therapeutic benefit from location or testimonials. |
+| BANK-077-039 | What does a subscription yoga platform need to disclose about personalization? | Check actual assessment inputs, algorithmic claims, instructor feedback and data handling; distinguish selectable preferences from clinically validated tailoring. |
+
+## 08. Evaluation and ethical wellness media
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-077-040 | How can a small community programme report outcomes honestly without running a clinical trial? | Describe attendance, consented feedback, missing responses and limitations; label service evaluation and avoid causal health claims from before-and-after satisfaction scores. |
+| BANK-077-041 | What should a yoga-content creator disclose when demonstrating an edited practice experience? | Identify omitted periods, instructor support, retakes and sponsorship; avoid presenting a curated transformation as typical participant evidence. |
+| BANK-077-042 | How can adverse experiences be included without implying that all yoga is harmful or harmless? | Use systematic reporting definitions, exposure information and qualified accounts; separate documented events, causal uncertainty and individual care decisions. |
+| BANK-077-043 | When should a wellness episode redirect a specific question to a qualified clinician? | Define the limits of public education around symptoms, diagnosis, medication and individualized adaptations; use current professional guidance rather than giving remote clearance. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
