+# 084 Collectibles & Antiques: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 31 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Collectibles & Antiques. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Objects, records and claims
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-013 | What separates an antique object's age from the date of the story attached to it? | Compare materials, construction, inscriptions and ownership records for a documented example; avoid treating family tradition or a seller's description as independent dating evidence. |
+| BANK-084-014 | How do collectible, vintage and antique labels vary by market and legal context? | Read dated trade usage and applicable official definitions; distinguish informal marketing terms from customs or regulatory categories. |
+| BANK-084-015 | What belongs in a basic object record before research or sale? | Document measurements, markings, condition, acquisition history and photographs using an owned item; exclude private addresses and unverified attribution as fact. |
+
+## 02. Paper, books and printed ephemera
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-016 | How can a book's edition be distinguished from its printing and later binding? | Inspect title page, publication statement, collation and bibliographic references; avoid calling every old copy a first edition or inferring value from age alone. |
+| BANK-084-017 | What can a historical postcard reveal beyond its picture? | Compare publisher, postal marks, message, alterations and distribution context; protect personal information and distinguish postmark date from image date. |
+| BANK-084-018 | Why can a signature require provenance and expert comparison rather than visual resemblance alone? | Trace documented ownership, reference exemplars and authentication limits; exclude forgery techniques and avoid certifying an autograph from a photograph. |
+| BANK-084-019 | How can a poster's reproduction status be investigated without damaging it? | Compare documented dimensions, printing method, paper and publication records with qualified references; exclude destructive tests and universal visual authenticity rules. |
+
+## 03. Coins, stamps and small-format collections
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-020 | What does a coin grade describe and leave outside its scope? | Review recognized grading definitions, surface condition and certification records; distinguish grade, authenticity, rarity and provenance without giving a personal price estimate. |
+| BANK-084-021 | Why can a cleaned coin be less desirable to some collectors despite looking brighter? | Use conservation and grading authorities to explain surface evidence and market preferences; exclude cleaning demonstrations or claims that every patina is original. |
+| BANK-084-022 | How can a stamp variety be distinguished from damage or printing variation? | Use authoritative catalogs, issuing records and professional identification methods; avoid reproducing deceptive alterations or inferring rarity from an online listing. |
+| BANK-084-023 | What makes a sports-card population report different from the number of surviving cards? | Inspect the grading service's methodology, submissions, resubmissions and coverage limits; avoid equating a reported slab count with total scarcity. |
+
+## 04. Ceramics, furniture and decorative objects
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-024 | How can a ceramics mark be researched without treating it as conclusive proof? | Compare mark dates, body, glaze, form and documented manufacturer records; note reproductions and avoid assigning origin from a single stamp. |
+| BANK-084-025 | What can furniture joinery reveal about construction and later alteration? | Use documented examples, tool traces and repair records; distinguish suggestive features from exact dating and exclude invasive examination of valuable objects. |
+| BANK-084-026 | Why can replacement parts change how a clock or mechanical collectible is described? | Map originality, function, service history and disclosure using qualified assessment; avoid implying that running condition proves historical completeness. |
+| BANK-084-027 | How can decorative wear be distinguished from damage requiring conservation advice? | Document location, pattern and material with professional references; avoid home restoration or declaring an object's safety from appearance alone. |
+
+## 05. Toys, games and popular-culture objects
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-028 | What distinguishes a toy's production version from a later reissue? | Compare manufacturer records, packaging, materials and documented variations; avoid treating an older-looking box as proof of original contents. |
+| BANK-084-029 | How can a game collection preserve the relationship between rules, pieces and editions? | Record component lists, publication dates, expansions and replacement parts; respect rights when reproducing manuals and distinguish complete playability from original condition. |
+| BANK-084-030 | Why can packaging shape collectible value without proving the object inside is authentic? | Compare condition definitions, seals, provenance and expert limitations; exclude resealing methods or claims of certainty based solely on unopened appearance. |
+| BANK-084-031 | How should a film-prop or memorabilia claim be checked? | Trace production records, documented custody and authorized identifiers; distinguish screen-used, production-made, replica and promotional objects rather than merging them as authentic. |
+
+## 06. Condition, preservation and collection care
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-032 | How can a collection inventory support disaster recovery without exposing security details? | Use private records of identification, condition and documentation; separate a useful ownership record from guaranteed insurance acceptance or public display of locations. |
+| BANK-084-033 | Why can one storage environment be unsuitable for a mixed-material collection? | Review light, moisture, pollutants and material compatibility from conservation institutions; avoid recommending one humidity target for every object. |
+| BANK-084-034 | What should happen before cleaning an unfamiliar inherited object? | Document condition, identify materials and seek qualified advice where needed; distinguish reversible dust management from removing evidence or applying untested products. |
+| BANK-084-035 | How can digital photographs preserve useful object information without replacing the physical record? | Specify scale, marks, angles, file metadata and backup; distinguish documentary images from scans that could establish hidden structure or authenticity. |
+
+## 07. Markets, valuation and transaction evidence
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-036 | How can auction results be compared without confusing estimates with total prices paid? | Separate hammer price, buyer fees, taxes, currency, date and unsold lots; avoid deriving a personalized valuation from a single result. |
+| BANK-084-037 | What does a recent sales history reveal that asking prices do not? | Compare actual transaction evidence, condition, attribution and venue; acknowledge selection bias and exclude guaranteed appreciation claims. |
+| BANK-084-038 | How can a provenance gap affect both value and the decision to transact? | Trace known custody, missing periods, title issues and current local rules; do not assume absence of records proves theft or legitimizes a purchase. |
+| BANK-084-039 | What should be disclosed when a creator values an object they also sell? | Identify ownership, commercial interest, evidence and uncertainty under applicable rules; distinguish editorial explanation from independent appraisal. |
+
+## 08. Cultural property, ethics and advanced attribution
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-084-040 | What should be verified before moving an antiquity across a border? | Consult current export, import, ownership and protected-cultural-property rules with documented provenance; exclude evasion routes or assumptions that a sales receipt establishes lawful export. |
+| BANK-084-041 | How do restitution claims differ from ordinary disputes over market authenticity? | Use official records, acquisition history and claimant perspectives for a named case; distinguish legal findings, ethical arguments and unresolved ownership. |
+| BANK-084-042 | Why can scientific material analysis narrow an attribution without identifying the maker? | Inspect published method, reference samples, contamination and uncertainty; distinguish material compatibility from proof of authorship or exact date. |
+| BANK-084-043 | How can a collection story include the makers and prior communities rather than only wealthy owners? | Trace production, labor, use and acquisition through attributed records and consented accounts; avoid inventing biographies to fill provenance gaps. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
