+# 085 DIY & Making: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for DIY & Making. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Designing a bounded making project
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-013 | How can a DIY project begin with a measured need instead of copying a finished photograph? | Develop an original small desk organizer from dimensions, use and constraints; separate a feasible brief from a structural or electrical design claim. |
+| BANK-085-014 | What does a prototype need to test before final materials are purchased? | Use paper or cardboard models to examine fit, access and assembly order; avoid treating a visual mockup as proof of strength or long-term durability. |
+| BANK-085-015 | How can a maker decide which dimensions actually require precision? | Compare functional fits, visual alignment and generous clearances in a harmless project; distinguish tolerance requirements from unnecessarily exact decorative measurements. |
+| BANK-085-016 | Why should a project plan include mistakes, cleanup and curing time? | Build an illustrative sequence with dependencies and material instructions; avoid presenting edited video duration as the time a beginner should expect. |
+
+## 02. Measuring, marking and joining
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-017 | How can repeated measurement errors accumulate across a simple assembly? | Trace datum choice, reference edges and cumulative variation using safe original models; distinguish measured evidence from assuming an expensive tool guarantees accuracy. |
+| BANK-085-018 | What should be compared before choosing glue, fasteners or a removable joint? | Examine materials, load description, reversibility and manufacturer guidance for a noncritical craft; exclude safety-critical or overhead installations. |
+| BANK-085-019 | Why does clamping pressure not solve every poorly fitted joint? | Compare surface contact, alignment, adhesive requirements and curing in documented examples; avoid improvised pressure rigs or claims that adhesive replaces structural assessment. |
+| BANK-085-020 | How can a full-size paper template reduce errors in a decorative project? | Test placement, symmetry, clearances and marking transfer using original designs; distinguish template accuracy from the suitability of the final material. |
+
+## 03. Paper, cardboard and textile projects
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-021 | What makes a cardboard organizer resist bending in ordinary desk use? | Compare folds, spans, material direction and low-load prototypes; label testing limits and avoid promoting cardboard for fire-sensitive or load-bearing uses. |
+| BANK-085-022 | How can a hand-sewn repair be planned around fabric condition rather than a fashionable stitch? | Inspect an owned nonprotective garment for edge stability, access and comfort; consult material guidance and exclude repairs to safety equipment. |
+| BANK-085-023 | What changes when a paper pattern is enlarged rather than redesigned for a larger object? | Compare thickness, folds, supports and assembly clearances in an original craft; avoid assuming every physical property scales linearly. |
+| BANK-085-024 | How can reusable fabric wraps be evaluated for the objects they will actually carry? | Compare size, fastening, washing instructions and modest loads using owned items; exclude food-contact or safety claims without appropriate material evidence. |
+
+## 04. Wood, finishes and material selection
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-025 | How do solid wood and sheet materials create different design constraints? | Compare grain, edges, thickness, documented moisture behavior and intended use; exclude structural furniture or machine-operation instructions requiring professional supervision. |
+| BANK-085-026 | Why can a finish look different on end grain, face grain and a previously coated surface? | Use labeled offcuts, manufacturer instructions and controlled viewing; do not prescribe solvent mixtures or assume unknown old coatings are safe to disturb. |
+| BANK-085-027 | What should a maker verify before using reclaimed material indoors? | Investigate provenance, contamination, fasteners, prior coatings and suitability through qualified guidance; exclude processing unknown hazardous material for a demonstration. |
+| BANK-085-028 | How can a small test piece prevent a larger project's surface treatment from failing? | Record preparation, product compatibility and drying conditions using the actual labeled materials; distinguish a test outcome from a guarantee for every substrate. |
+
+## 05. Tools, workspaces and task boundaries
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-029 | What can a beginner's workspace plan establish before a cutting or drilling task? | Review manufacturer requirements, stable workholding, clearances, lighting and qualified instruction; keep the episode at planning level and exclude bypassing guards or protections. |
+| BANK-085-030 | Why does a drill bit's compatibility matter beyond fitting in the chuck? | Explain material, diameter, tool limits and manufacturer specifications without providing hazardous drilling procedures; exclude walls with unknown utilities and safety-critical applications. |
+| BANK-085-031 | How can dust-control claims be checked before working with a particular material? | Consult material safety data, equipment instructions and occupational guidance; distinguish visible cleanup from verified exposure control and avoid a DIY respirator substitute. |
+| BANK-085-032 | When should a household repair stop being a DIY project? | Map uncertainty, permits, hazardous materials and consequences of failure using official local guidance; exclude mains wiring, gas, critical plumbing and structural-work instructions. |
+
+## 06. Reuse, repair and project economics
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-033 | How can a DIY budget account for tools and failed attempts as well as materials? | Use transparent illustrative quantities, consumables, rentals and contingency; distinguish first-project cost from later reuse and avoid claiming making is always cheaper. |
+| BANK-085-034 | What does repairing a noncritical household object require before trying an adhesive fix? | Identify material, use, existing damage and replacement options through manufacturer guidance; exclude food-contact, electrical, pressurized or load-bearing repairs. |
+| BANK-085-035 | How can a maker compare reuse with buying new without inventing environmental savings? | Define function, expected life, transport and material inputs; label missing lifecycle evidence rather than assuming every reused object has lower impact. |
+| BANK-085-036 | Why can disassembly planning improve an object's usefulness after the first project? | Compare removable joints, replaceable parts and material separation in an original low-risk design; avoid promising recyclability without local acceptance evidence. |
+
+## 07. Documentation, troubleshooting and design literacy
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-037 | How can a tutorial show failed attempts without teaching an unsafe workaround? | Explain the cause, evidence and revised low-risk design using original footage; remove hazardous demonstrations and clearly identify untested ideas. |
+| BANK-085-038 | What should a cut list or material list specify so another maker can assess it? | Include dimensions, units, grade, substitutions and assumptions for a harmless craft; avoid implying that a list certifies engineering adequacy. |
+| BANK-085-039 | How can a finished project be tested against its original purpose? | Define modest intended use, inspection and repeatable observations; distinguish a bounded demonstration from strength certification or permission for heavier loads. |
+| BANK-085-040 | What makes a good troubleshooting guide branch on observations rather than guessed causes? | Build a decision map for a low-risk assembly problem with reversible checks; exclude advice to keep using damaged equipment or bypass safety controls. |
+
+## 08. Rights, access and sharing
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-085-041 | What should a maker check before selling an object based on someone else's pattern? | Read the actual pattern license, commercial terms and applicable local rights rules; distinguish attribution from permission and avoid assuming online availability grants resale rights. |
+| BANK-085-042 | How can a DIY demonstration be made accessible without claiming one adaptation fits everyone? | Use consented task needs, readable measurements, captions and alternative tools where qualified; preserve safety requirements rather than improvising inaccessible-equipment workarounds. |
+| BANK-085-043 | What must be disclosed when a tutorial includes sponsored tools or materials? | Identify gifts, payment, affiliate relationships and the exact tested setup under applicable rules; separate a product demonstration from independent comparative testing. |
+| BANK-085-044 | How can digital fabrication files be shared with enough context for responsible reuse? | Document units, material assumptions, versions and intended low-risk application; exclude dangerous designs and do not treat a downloadable model as manufacturing certification. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
