+# 086 Restoration: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Restoration. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Purpose and initial assessment
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-013 | How do conservation, restoration and repair define different goals for the same object? | Compare retained evidence, intended use and acceptable change through a documented noncritical object; distinguish professional conservation ethics from making something look new. |
+| BANK-086-014 | What should be documented before any restoration work begins? | Record materials, dimensions, marks, damage, previous repairs and ownership permissions; use an owned object and avoid assigning an attribution not supported by evidence. |
+| BANK-086-015 | Why can a functioning object still be unsuitable for restoration by a hobbyist? | Map hidden hazards, significance, failure consequences and specialist assessment needs; exclude energizing unknown equipment or dismantling safety-critical items. |
+| BANK-086-016 | How can an owner decide which changes should remain visible? | Compare maker intent, use history, sentimental meaning and conservation advice; distinguish agreed treatment goals from a universal demand for a pristine appearance. |
+
+## 02. Condition, materials and diagnosis
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-017 | What distinguishes surface dirt from a layer that belongs to an object's history? | Use qualified conservation examples and material examination; avoid removing deposits to discover their meaning or assuming every dark layer is expendable grime. |
+| BANK-086-018 | How can corrosion be described without assuming all metal deterioration behaves alike? | Compare identified materials, documented corrosion products and environmental context; exclude chemical treatment recipes and diagnosis from color alone. |
+| BANK-086-019 | Why can a cracked wooden object change with its storage environment? | Review wood movement, grain, prior construction and documented environmental history; distinguish plausible contributors from a complete cause established by one photograph. |
+| BANK-086-020 | What can ultraviolet or magnified examination reveal and leave uncertain? | Use published professional methods, recorded conditions and interpretation limits; do not equate fluorescence or magnification with proof of age, authorship or authenticity. |
+
+## 03. Furniture and wooden objects
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-021 | How can a loose furniture joint be assessed before deciding to reglue it? | Inspect construction, old adhesive, missing material and intended use through professional guidance; exclude structural seating repair instructions or unqualified load testing. |
+| BANK-086-022 | What does veneer lifting reveal about more than the visible top layer? | Compare substrate, adhesive, moisture history and previous repairs in documented cases; avoid pressing or heating an unknown antique as a universal solution. |
+| BANK-086-023 | Why can stripping an old finish remove useful evidence? | Trace finish layers, wear, tool marks and historical appearance through conservation records; exclude disturbance of unknown hazardous coatings. |
+| BANK-086-024 | How should replacement wood be documented in a restored object? | Record species evidence, location, joining method and visual distinction with permission; avoid presenting new material as untouched original fabric. |
+
+## 04. Paper, books and textiles
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-025 | What should be assessed before trying to flatten a folded historical document? | Consult paper-conservation guidance on ink, support, moisture sensitivity and significance; exclude household heat or humidity treatments for unknown materials. |
+| BANK-086-026 | Why can adhesive tape create a longer conservation problem than the original tear? | Use institutional conservation references on aging, staining and removal complexity; do not demonstrate solvents or repair valuable documents with untested products. |
+| BANK-086-027 | How do book conservation decisions differ when the binding is itself historically important? | Compare structure, use, provenance and treatment records for a named example; distinguish repair for access from rebuilding a preferred appearance. |
+| BANK-086-028 | What makes cleaning a historic textile different from laundering a modern garment? | Examine fiber, dye, construction, damage and professional tests; exclude washing recipes or claims of safety based only on a care label from another object. |
+
+## 05. Metals, ceramics and composite objects
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-029 | How can polishing alter the information available on a metal object? | Compare inscriptions, tool marks, plating and historic surfaces using documented treatment examples; do not assume increased shine improves conservation or value. |
+| BANK-086-030 | Why does a repaired ceramic object's intended use need to be stated explicitly? | Distinguish display, handling, food contact and structural integrity with qualified guidance; exclude claims that an adhesive repair restores food safety or original strength. |
+| BANK-086-031 | What can missing fragments teach a restorer about reconstruction limits? | Map surviving evidence, reference objects and unknown form; label fills and conjecture instead of manufacturing an undocumented complete original. |
+| BANK-086-032 | How do composite materials create conflicts for a single cleaning method? | Use a documented object combining wood, metal or textile to compare sensitivities; avoid applying one treatment to every component for visual consistency. |
+
+## 06. Mechanical and electronic heritage
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-033 | What is lost when a historic machine is made to run with modern replacement parts? | Compare function, evidence, wear and documentation using a professionally managed example; exclude operating unknown machinery or bypassing protective systems. |
+| BANK-086-034 | How can a restoration film explain an old radio without powering it on? | Use schematics, provenance, external inspection and expert explanation; distinguish functional claims from appearance and exclude high-voltage troubleshooting procedures. |
+| BANK-086-035 | Why should old batteries and unknown electrical components be treated as separate assessment problems? | Consult manufacturer, hazardous-material and qualified repair guidance; exclude charging, opening or experimentally reusing degraded components. |
+| BANK-086-036 | What does digital documentation preserve when a device's original software or media no longer works? | Compare hardware records, legal archival access, file formats and emulation limits; avoid bypassing rights protections or claiming a simulation reproduces every original behavior. |
+
+## 07. Treatment planning and professional ethics
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-037 | What does reversibility mean when a treatment cannot literally be undone without a trace? | Examine conservation standards, retreatability, documentation and material change through published cases; avoid using reversible as an unsupported marketing guarantee. |
+| BANK-086-038 | How can the least-intervention principle conflict with an owner's wish to keep using an object? | Compare significance, wear, access and informed consent; distinguish ethical tradeoffs from a rule that all objects must be retired from use. |
+| BANK-086-039 | What evidence should justify removing an earlier repair? | Inspect its history, stability, harm and effect on interpretation with professional assessment; do not assume an unattractive repair has no heritage value. |
+| BANK-086-040 | How can restoration costs be discussed without promising an increase in resale price? | Separate labor, materials, specialist tests, risk and intended outcome using illustrative figures; distinguish treatment value from a speculative market valuation. |
+
+## 08. Honest restoration media and handover
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-086-041 | How can before-and-after images avoid exaggerating a restoration's success? | Use consistent light, scale, angles and disclosure of replaced parts; distinguish a visual comparison from proof of structural stability or authenticity. |
+| BANK-086-042 | What should a restoration video disclose when corrosion, dirt or damage was recreated for filming? | Label staged material and separate it from the object's verified condition; avoid fabricated discovery narratives or presenting destructive preparation as conservation. |
+| BANK-086-043 | How can an owner receive a useful record after treatment? | Provide condition notes, materials, changes, limitations and qualified care recommendations; distinguish documented work from a guarantee against future deterioration. |
+| BANK-086-044 | When does an object need referral rather than another experiment? | Map significance, unstable materials, hazardous components and failed prior attempts using professional guidance; exclude further invasive trials on unknown or valuable items. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
