+| BANK-087-042 | How can a failed mechanism reveal the limits of an ideal diagram? | Use a documented harmless case to compare friction, tolerances, wear and conditions; do not operate damaged equipment to create dramatic footage. |
+| BANK-087-043 | Why can feedback control oscillate rather than settle immediately at its target? | Use a clearly labeled software simulation of sensor delay and response; separate conceptual behavior from a deployable controller for real machinery. |
+| BANK-087-044 | What evidence is needed before claiming a device violates an ordinary physical limit? | Define the claimed output, inputs, measurement boundaries and independent tests; avoid promoting unverified free-energy or perpetual-motion claims. |
+| BANK-087-045 | How can a cutaway animation show hidden parts without inventing a mechanism? | Base geometry and motion on public engineering records, label simplifications and preserve uncertainty; distinguish representative illustration from the exact product design. |
