+| BANK-088-032 | How can a chocolate-production film distinguish cocoa processing from making a finished bar? | Trace documented fermentation context, roasting, refining, conching and molding with product variation explicit; exclude unsupported food-safety or nutrition claims. |
+| BANK-088-033 | What changes between milled flour and a packaged commercial bread product? | Use authorized bakery flow records for mixing, fermentation, baking, cooling and packaging; distinguish explanation from a shelf-life or allergen-safety guarantee. |
+| BANK-088-034 | Why does soap manufacture involve chemistry that should not be copied from a factory montage? | Explain documented material transformation and industrial quality controls at a conceptual level; exclude caustic formulations or home-production instructions. |
+| BANK-088-035 | How can a pencil's simple appearance hide several separate material-production steps? | Follow documented graphite mixture, wood preparation, assembly and finishing; distinguish the graphite core from a misleading claim that it contains metallic lead. |
+
+## 07. Craft and industrial-scale comparisons
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-088-036 | How do handmade and automated production differ beyond output per hour? | Compare skill, variation, material use, quality criteria and labor in one named product; avoid assuming hand work is always better or automation eliminates expertise. |
+| BANK-088-037 | What changes when a prototype is manufactured in ten units versus ten thousand? | Trace tooling, process validation, procurement and inspection in an explicitly illustrative case; distinguish cost modeling from actual supplier quotations. |
+| BANK-088-038 | How can a production film represent workers whose tasks are repetitive or visually quiet? | Use consented accounts, decision points and maintenance or quality roles; avoid filming employees without permission or reducing labor to machine attendance. |
+| BANK-088-039 | Why can two facilities make the same product through different process routes? | Compare scale, equipment, inputs and specified performance using authorized records; distinguish route differences from a claim that one facility is unsafe. |
+
+## 08. Environmental claims and production transparency
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-088-040 | How can a how-it-is-made episode account for waste without relying on a clean factory image? | Trace scrap, rejects, byproducts and documented destinations within explicit boundaries; avoid treating collected waste as verified recycling. |
+| BANK-088-041 | What must be checked before describing a production line as closed loop? | Define material and energy inputs, losses, recovery quality and reporting period from primary records; distinguish partial recirculation from zero waste. |
+| BANK-088-042 | How can commercial confidentiality be respected without hiding which claims were not independently observed? | Mark filmed stages, supplied diagrams, restricted areas and unverified manufacturer statements; avoid presenting promotional footage as an independent audit. |
+| BANK-088-043 | What does a finished-product traceability record need to connect across suppliers? | Map batch identity, material records, process stages and test evidence for one bounded chain; distinguish recordkeeping from proof of every sustainability or labor claim. |
