+# 097 Government & Public Systems: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Government & Public Systems. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Institutions, authority and public functions
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-013 | How can a viewer distinguish the state, government and public administration in one jurisdiction? | Map constitutional roles, elected offices and administrative bodies using current official texts; do not assume terms transfer unchanged across countries. |
+| BANK-097-014 | What changes between a public policy announcement and an enforceable rule? | Trace legal authority, approval, publication, commencement and implementation in a documented case; distinguish intentions from duties already in force. |
+| BANK-097-015 | How do national, regional and local responsibilities divide a public service? | Use official powers, budgets and operating arrangements for one service; separate formal responsibility from actual delivery partnerships. |
+| BANK-097-016 | Why can an agency perform several roles that appear contradictory to citizens? | Compare its statutory mandate, resources, procedures and accountability; avoid attributing failure or bad intent without records. |
+
+## 02. Budgets, taxation and spending
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-017 | How does a public budget move from proposal to actual expenditure? | Trace authorization, allocation, release, procurement and audited spending in a named fiscal year; distinguish announced totals from cash used. |
+| BANK-097-018 | What does a tax-funded service cost measure if users pay no direct fee? | Compare operating costs, capital, eligibility and financing using official accounts; avoid treating free at point of use as costless. |
+| BANK-097-019 | Why can a department underspend its allocation while demand remains unmet? | Inspect staffing, procurement, release timing and documented constraints; distinguish plausible explanations from audit findings. |
+| BANK-097-020 | How should a public-debt figure be read alongside interest, maturity and currency? | Use official definitions, consolidation boundaries and dated data; exclude personal financial advice or a universal threshold for crisis. |
+
+## 03. Service journeys and implementation
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-021 | How can an application process be mapped from a citizen's first question to its outcome? | Choose a named service and use current forms, official timelines and consented accounts; distinguish written procedure from observed access. |
+| BANK-097-022 | What can a grievance system resolve that an appeal process cannot? | Read the service's official powers, deadlines and remedies; avoid telling a particular person which legal route will succeed. |
+| BANK-097-023 | Why can a digital-only public service exclude people who technically have internet access? | Compare identity requirements, language, devices, skills and assistance using ethical local evidence; do not equate coverage with usable access. |
+| BANK-097-024 | How can a benefit programme's eligibility be explained without deciding an individual's entitlement? | Use current official criteria, exclusions, dates and application channels; keep examples hypothetical and avoid guarantees of approval. |
+
+## 04. Procurement, infrastructure and maintenance
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-025 | How does public procurement differ from selecting the cheapest advertised product? | Inspect applicable official rules, specifications, competition, evaluation and contract management; distinguish policy rationale from proof of compliance in a case. |
+| BANK-097-026 | What records help explain why a public project changed cost or completion date? | Compare approved scope, variations, contracts, audits and actual milestones; avoid assuming every overrun proves corruption or was unavoidable. |
+| BANK-097-027 | Why should a new public facility's budget include maintenance after inauguration? | Trace staffing, utilities, renewal and operating responsibility with official records; distinguish completed construction from sustained service delivery. |
+| BANK-097-028 | How can a performance-based service contract be assessed beyond its stated target? | Inspect measurement, exclusions, verification, penalties and user outcomes; avoid treating a contractual incentive as proof of improved quality. |
+
+## 05. Data, identity and administrative decisions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-029 | What does an administrative database measure differently from a representative survey? | Compare coverage, eligibility, updates, duplicates and missing populations; do not treat registered cases as a complete population census. |
+| BANK-097-030 | How can an automated public-service decision be examined for accountability? | Identify inputs, official decision rules, human review, explanation and appeal rights; avoid claiming an algorithm is fair from accuracy alone. |
+| BANK-097-031 | What should an open-data portal disclose about a published dataset? | Check definitions, date, revisions, geographic coverage and reuse terms; distinguish downloadable data from reliable or complete measurement. |
+| BANK-097-032 | Why can linking public records create privacy concerns even when each dataset is public? | Map identifiability, purpose, access and current law; use fictional records rather than reidentifying real people. |
+
+## 06. Oversight, audits and integrity
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-033 | How do financial, compliance and performance audits ask different questions? | Compare official audit mandates and published reports; distinguish an audit observation from a criminal finding or a complete verdict on a programme. |
+| BANK-097-034 | What does a parliamentary or legislative committee add to executive oversight? | Trace mandate, hearings, evidence and response requirements in a named system; avoid assuming recommendations automatically become law. |
+| BANK-097-035 | How can a corruption allegation be investigated through public evidence without repeating rumor? | Build a dated record of contracts, official inquiries and court findings; attribute allegations and preserve unresolved status. |
+| BANK-097-036 | What can freedom-of-information records establish and still leave unanswered? | Review the actual disclosure, scope, exemptions and missing material; distinguish a partial response from proof that no other records exist. |
+
+## 07. Public participation and emergency governance
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-037 | What makes a public consultation meaningful beyond collecting responses? | Inspect who could participate, accessible information, feedback handling and documented changes; distinguish participation volume from representativeness or influence. |
+| BANK-097-038 | How can disaster-management responsibilities be explained before an emergency? | Use current official local plans, agency roles and accessible communication routes; exclude forecasting events or inventing operational instructions. |
+| BANK-097-039 | Why can emergency powers require separate scrutiny from ordinary administration? | Read the exact legal authority, duration, oversight and limits for a named case; avoid broad conclusions that every emergency action is lawful. |
+| BANK-097-040 | How can a city service include residents whose addresses are informal or changing? | Examine current rules, alternative documentation and consented experiences; do not expose vulnerable locations or invent eligibility exemptions. |
+
+## 08. Comparative government and evaluated outcomes
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-097-041 | How can two countries' public services be compared without ignoring different responsibilities? | Align functions, populations, financing and outcome definitions before comparing performance; avoid ranking systems from incompatible headline metrics. |
+| BANK-097-042 | What distinguishes a programme evaluation from evidence that participants liked the service? | Compare counterfactual design, implementation, follow-up and missing data; separate satisfaction from measured causal outcomes. |
+| BANK-097-043 | Why can a successful pilot fail when adopted across a government system? | Investigate staff capacity, funding, selection, incentives and local variation using original evaluations; avoid attributing scale failure to one unsupported cause. |
+| BANK-097-044 | How should a policy explainer update when the rules change after publication? | Date the original scope, identify amendments and revise actionable details; preserve historical explanation without presenting superseded instructions as current. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
