+# 098 Law & Justice: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 33 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Law & Justice. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Reading law in context
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-098-013 | How can a legal explainer distinguish a statute, regulation and court judgment? | Use current official examples from one jurisdiction to map authority and purpose; avoid assuming the hierarchy is identical everywhere. |
+| BANK-098-014 | What information is needed before asking which law applies to an event? | Identify jurisdiction, date, relevant conduct and procedural context through fictional examples; do not decide an individual's legal position. |
+| BANK-098-015 | Why can the same legal word have different definitions in different statutes? | Compare actual definitions and purpose in official texts; avoid importing an everyday meaning or another jurisdiction's definition without checking. |
+| BANK-098-016 | How should a viewer distinguish legal information from advice on a personal dispute? | Compare a general rule, necessary facts and professional interpretation using hypothetical cases; exclude personalized litigation or compliance conclusions. |
+
+## 02. Courts, procedure and evidence
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-098-017 | How do trial and appellate courts ask different questions in a named court system? | Use official jurisdiction and procedure guides; distinguish factual review, legal review and remedies without promising a route for a real case. |
+| BANK-098-018 | What changes between an allegation, a charge, a finding and a final appeal outcome? | Trace a documented public case with dated official records; preserve procedural status and avoid treating accusation as guilt. |
+| BANK-098-019 | How can burden and standard of proof be explained without mixing civil and criminal processes? | Compare the exact jurisdiction's official rules and hypothetical examples; avoid exporting one standard to every proceeding. |
+| BANK-098-020 | Why can relevant material still face limits on admissibility? | Examine a bounded evidence rule, authentication and procedural safeguards using official sources; do not advise how to introduce evidence in an individual's case. |
+| BANK-098-021 | What does a court order require before it can be treated as the final outcome of a dispute? | Inspect scope, interim status, appeal, stay and enforcement records; avoid reporting an early procedural order as a final merits decision. |
+
+## 03. Contracts and ordinary transactions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-098-022 | What should a contract explainer inspect beyond the signature page? | Read obligations, definitions, conditions, termination, remedies and governing law in a fictional agreement; do not certify enforceability. |
+| BANK-098-023 | How can an online service's terms differ from its advertising claims? | Compare dated official terms, checkout disclosures and applicable consumer rules; distinguish a marketing statement from a completed legal finding. |
+| BANK-098-024 | Why can a refund policy and statutory consumer rights be different questions? | Use current official local law and an illustrative transaction; avoid deciding entitlement or assuming the store policy overrides every legal protection. |
+| BANK-098-025 | What does contractual consent require in a context with standard-form terms? | Inspect applicable doctrine, notice and official decisions in a named jurisdiction; distinguish a click from a universal legal conclusion about assent. |
+
+## 04. Rights, public law and access to justice
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
