+# 099 Intelligence & Espionage: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**9 categories · 34 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Intelligence & Espionage. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Intelligence as an institution
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-013 | How does intelligence analysis differ from ordinary news reporting in a documented institutional context? | Compare mandate, audience, classified access and assessment products using public official records; avoid inventing secret procedures. |
+| BANK-099-014 | What distinguishes intelligence collection, analysis and policy decisions? | Trace responsibilities in a declassified case; keep the assessment separate from what leaders chose to do. |
+| BANK-099-015 | How can an espionage documentary define what is actually known at the outset? | Build a dated inventory of declassified records, court findings and attributed testimony; label remaining classification and disputed claims. |
+
+## 02. Archives and declassification
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-016 | What does a declassified document's release history reveal about the evidence available? | Inspect creation date, redactions, review date and archival context; distinguish partial release from a complete operational record. |
+| BANK-099-017 | Why can a memoir conflict with contemporary intelligence records? | Compare timing, access, incentives and corroboration in a published case; do not assume either secrecy or personal detail guarantees truth. |
+| BANK-099-018 | How can forged or misattributed historical documents distort an intelligence story? | Trace provenance, archival authentication and official findings; exclude fabrication techniques and avoid certifying documents from appearance alone. |
+| BANK-099-019 | What should a documentary do when a dramatic claim rests on a single anonymous account? | Assess corroboration, access and attribution limits; present it as an unresolved claim rather than filling gaps with cinematic certainty. |
+
+## 03. Historical cases and bounded questions
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-020 | What can official inquiries into Pearl Harbor reveal about warning and interpretation? | Compare dated information, organizational responsibilities and inquiry findings; distinguish retrospective knowledge from what decision makers had available. |
+| BANK-099-021 | How did published investigations explain intelligence use during the Cuban Missile Crisis? | Use declassified assessments, official timelines and attributed participant records; avoid claiming one image or individual alone determined the outcome. |
+| BANK-099-022 | What do public records of the Cambridge spy cases establish about institutional vulnerabilities? | Use official archives and documented investigations; distinguish verified acts from later speculation and exclude recruitment or concealment guidance. |
+| BANK-099-023 | How can the history of Bletchley Park include organizational labor beyond famous codebreakers? | Use official historical records, job accounts and consented oral histories; distinguish public explanation of historical roles from operational cryptanalytic instruction. |
+
+## 04. Assessment, uncertainty and failure
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-024 | What does an intelligence estimate's confidence language mean in its own published methodology? | Read the actual official definitions and assessment context; do not convert qualitative wording into invented numeric probabilities. |
+| BANK-099-025 | How can an intelligence failure be separated into collection, interpretation and communication questions? | Use a documented inquiry to identify supported findings and alternatives; avoid hindsight-based claims that the result was obvious. |
+| BANK-099-026 | Why can the absence of a warning in released records fail to prove that no warning existed? | Examine archival coverage, retention, redaction and institutional boundaries; distinguish missing evidence from a theory of deliberate concealment. |
+| BANK-099-027 | What can competing hypotheses contribute to analysis of incomplete information? | Use a harmless fictional historical-style dataset and published methods; avoid targeting real people or producing operational intelligence. |
+
+## 05. Oversight, law and civil liberties
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-028 | How do intelligence oversight bodies obtain and limit their authority? | Read current official legislation, committee mandates and public reports for one jurisdiction; avoid assuming oversight arrangements are globally interchangeable. |
+| BANK-099-029 | What can a court decision establish about a surveillance programme? | Use the official judgment, scope, facts and later legal changes; distinguish legality findings from proof about every technical implementation. |
+| BANK-099-030 | How should a documentary discuss whistleblowing without resolving a real person's legal duties? | Compare applicable public law, official findings and attributed perspectives; avoid soliciting classified material or advising covert disclosure. |
+| BANK-099-031 | Why can a legal authorization and a public-interest justification be separate debates? | Define the actual programme, authority and ethical arguments with sources; avoid implying either discussion alone settles all consequences. |
+
+## 06. Technology and publicly documented capabilities
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-032 | How can satellite imagery contribute evidence without revealing intentions by itself? | Use publicly released historical examples, resolution limits and interpretation context; exclude current targeting or surveillance of private individuals. |
+| BANK-099-033 | What distinguishes metadata from message content in a public policy debate? | Use official definitions, a fictional example and documented privacy implications; avoid collection instructions or unauthorized access. |
+| BANK-099-034 | How should a claimed intelligence technology be evaluated when technical details remain secret? | Compare demonstrated public capability, official claims and independent evidence limits; do not invent performance or infer omniscience from secrecy. |
+| BANK-099-035 | What does encryption history reveal about the changing relationship between communications and government authority? | Trace published standards, policy records and dated cases; keep historical explanation separate from evasion or intrusion guidance. |
+
+## 07. Counterintelligence narratives and media ethics
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-036 | How can a spy film distinguish composite characters from documented historical people? | Label invented scenes, merged roles and verified events; avoid presenting dramatic dialogue as recovered testimony. |
+| BANK-099-037 | What must be established before describing a living person as an intelligence operative? | Require official public records or well-corroborated attributable evidence and careful status wording; exclude doxxing or speculation based on nationality, travel or employment. |
+| BANK-099-038 | Why can a cleared or unproven allegation remain misleading in old titles and thumbnails? | Update visible claims, chronology and outcomes; do not preserve an accusation's implied certainty merely because the narration includes a caveat. |
+| BANK-099-039 | How can a documentary portray an alleged double agent without assuming access to their inner motives? | Compare verified actions, contemporaneous statements and later interpretations; label motive claims and avoid invented psychological diagnosis. |
+
+## 08. Intelligence, diplomacy and historical consequences
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Define the rival claims and their evidence standards. Compare sources on equal terms, separate empirical findings from values or interpretations and do not imply that all positions have equal evidential support.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the original sources behind the compared claims; explicit definitions and measurement methods; independent critiques with traceable evidence. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-040 | How can an intelligence success be evaluated beyond the agency's own retrospective account? | Compare available information, decisions, corroborated outcomes and counterfactual limits; distinguish a useful assessment from proof it alone caused success. |
+| BANK-099-041 | What can public records reveal about intelligence cooperation between states? | Trace agreements, official inquiries and acknowledged information sharing in one historical case; avoid reconstructing current covert channels. |
+| BANK-099-042 | How can an intelligence history include civilians affected by an operation? | Use official investigations and consented accounts with identity protection; distinguish documented harms from unsupported casualty or responsibility claims. |
+| BANK-099-043 | What should an episode conclude when the central secret remains classified? | Resolve the supported institutional and historical questions, inventory missing evidence and preserve uncertainty; do not replace an unavailable answer with conspiracy. |
+
+## 09. Open sources and verification boundaries
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-099-044 | How can publicly available material be verified without turning research into surveillance? | Use authorized archives, provenance checks and nonpersonal examples; exclude location tracking, identity exposure and collection of sensitive personal data. |
+| BANK-099-045 | Why can a viral image be genuine while its claimed date or context is false? | Compare source history, metadata limits and authoritative records using a non-sensitive example; avoid identifying private subjects. |
+| BANK-099-046 | What distinguishes an official acknowledgement from a media report citing unnamed officials? | Trace publication, attribution, wording and later corroboration; do not merge different evidence levels into one statement of certainty. |
