+# 100 Forensics & Investigation: Detailed Topic-Bank Draft
+
+**8 categories · 32 individually authored episode proposals.**
+
+Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for Forensics & Investigation. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
+
+[All-niche progress](../DEPTH_COMPLETION_STATUS.md) · [All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable bank](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json)
+
+Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources and current niche angle scopes have not been verified. Learning levels organize documentary research rather than physical difficulty. The older initial proposals remain in the JSON's prior_initial_map archive and are not counted again.
+
+## 01. Evidence and the investigation question
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-013 | What makes a forensic finding relevant to one question but insufficient for another? | Separate material identity, source and activity propositions through fictional examples; avoid treating a match as automatic proof of guilt. |
+| BANK-100-014 | How does chain of custody support evidence integrity without establishing what the evidence means? | Use official procedures and a fictional record to compare handling, transfer and interpretation; do not certify a real item's admissibility. |
+| BANK-100-015 | Why can contamination matter even when an instrument measures accurately? | Compare collection context, controls, transport and laboratory handling in published methods; exclude tampering or concealment instructions. |
+| BANK-100-016 | What does a forensic laboratory's accreditation establish and leave outside its scope? | Read the actual standard and accredited methods; distinguish quality-system assessment from a guarantee that every conclusion is correct. |
+
+## 02. DNA and biological evidence
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-017 | What does a DNA association say differently from how the material arrived at a location? | Use published forensic guidance on source and activity questions; avoid naming suspects or making case-specific guilt claims. |
+| BANK-100-018 | How can a DNA mixture create interpretation questions absent from a single-source sample? | Explain contributors, uncertainty, model assumptions and validation at a conceptual level; exclude methods for defeating collection or testing. |
+| BANK-100-019 | Why must a forensic probability identify the competing propositions it compares? | Use a clearly fictional numeric example and original statistical guidance; distinguish likelihood ratios from the probability that a person is guilty. |
+| BANK-100-020 | What should a report disclose when biological material is too limited for a strong conclusion? | Inspect validated reporting categories, uncertainty and qualified testimony; avoid presenting inconclusive results as either exclusion or confirmation. |
+
+## 03. Fingerprints, marks and physical comparison
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-021 | How can a fingerprint comparison be explained without claiming infallibility? | Review original validation studies, examination process and reporting limits; distinguish examiner conclusions from universal error-free identification. |
+| BANK-100-022 | What does a footwear impression reveal beyond a possible brand or model? | Compare class features, wear, distortion and documentation in published methods; avoid individual attribution from a low-quality image. |
+| BANK-100-023 | Why can toolmark similarity require evidence about alternative sources? | Use official method evaluations and uncertainty studies; keep explanation nonoperational and exclude instructions for altering or concealing marks. |
+| BANK-100-024 | How should disputed comparison methods be reported when courts and scientific evaluations differ? | Separate admissibility decisions, empirical validation and expert disagreement; do not assume court acceptance proves scientific certainty. |
+
+## 04. Chemistry, toxicology and trace materials
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-025 | What distinguishes detecting a substance from determining its role in an event? | Compare sampling, concentration, timing and context using authoritative forensic sources; exclude poisoning details or case-specific medical interpretation. |
+| BANK-100-026 | How can a trace-material comparison narrow possibilities without uniquely identifying an origin? | Review fibers, paint or glass through published methods, reference data and limitations; avoid equating similarity with a complete provenance chain. |
+| BANK-100-027 | Why can a toxicology screen and a confirmatory test answer different questions? | Inspect intended use, sensitivity, specificity and laboratory reporting guidance; do not interpret a real person's result or prescribe treatment. |
+| BANK-100-028 | What can fire-debris analysis establish without independently explaining how a fire began? | Use official method documentation and investigation standards at a conceptual level; exclude ignition recipes or techniques for defeating detection. |
+
+## 05. Scenes, reconstruction and timing
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-029 | How can a scene reconstruction distinguish measured geometry from assumptions about movement? | Use a fictional layout with recorded dimensions, alternatives and uncertainty; avoid turning animation into proof of an unobserved sequence. |
+| BANK-100-030 | Why can estimating time since death require ranges and multiple kinds of evidence? | Consult current professional methods and original studies on variability; exclude calculations for real cases or sensational certainty from one sign. |
+| BANK-100-031 | What does a bloodstain-pattern opinion need to disclose about method and limits? | Review published validation, assumptions and documented scene context; avoid generating practical violence or evidence-alteration instructions. |
+| BANK-100-032 | How can accident investigation separate damage evidence from a conclusion about responsibility? | Compare official measurements, event data, standards and alternative sequences; keep legal fault distinct from physical reconstruction. |
+
+## 06. Digital records and authentication
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Inspect the actual product version, official documentation, terms and privacy policies. Test claims under stated conditions and distinguish account permissions, data retention, measured functionality and marketing.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official versioned documentation and release notes; dated privacy policies and service terms; reproducible product tests and original validation reports. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-033 | What does a cryptographic hash establish about a digital file? | Explain identical bytes and integrity checks with original harmless files; distinguish content integrity from proof of authorship or truthful content. |
+| BANK-100-034 | Why can a timestamp be unreliable without knowing how a device recorded it? | Compare clock settings, time zones, file operations and official technical documentation; exclude altering real evidence or evading investigation. |
+| BANK-100-035 | How can an investigator assess whether a screenshot faithfully represents a record? | Use published authentication methods and a fictional message example; distinguish appearance, source records and corroboration without identifying private users. |
+| BANK-100-036 | What should a digital-forensics report disclose about the tool and data extraction? | Inspect version, validation, permissions, missing data and reproducibility in official guidance; exclude unauthorized access or unlocking procedures. |
+
+## 07. Testimony, statistics and miscarriages of justice
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-037 | How can a jury-facing explanation avoid confusing a rare match with certainty of guilt? | Use official statistical guidance, explicit populations and hypothetical examples; distinguish evidence weight from the full case assessment. |
+| BANK-100-038 | What do official reviews of wrongful convictions reveal about overstated forensic testimony? | Choose documented cases with judgments and inquiry records; separate established errors from allegations and protect affected people. |
+| BANK-100-039 | How can an expert acknowledge uncertainty without implying that all conclusions are equally weak? | Compare validated result categories, strength of support and alternative explanations; avoid inventing numerical confidence where none is justified. |
+| BANK-100-040 | Why can disclosure of underlying data matter to evaluating an expert's conclusion? | Use current official procedural rules and method records in a named jurisdiction; do not offer individualized litigation strategy. |
+
+## 08. Ethical forensic media and research literacy
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-100-041 | How should a crime documentary label an illustrative laboratory demonstration? | Separate staged samples, real case findings and general method explanation; obtain permissions and avoid implying access to actual evidence. |
+| BANK-100-042 | What does an error-rate study need before its results can support a public claim? | Inspect task design, participants, ground truth, uncertainty and relevance to practice; do not transfer a rate blindly to a different method or case. |
+| BANK-100-043 | How can a forensic episode respect victims while questioning an official conclusion? | Use primary records, attributed experts and careful status wording; avoid graphic sensationalism, private evidence exposure or directing audiences at suspects. |
+| BANK-100-044 | When should a forensic mystery remain unresolved in the final edit? | Identify missing records, untested assumptions and limits of public evidence; do not replace an unsupported answer with a dramatic accusation. |
+
+## Coverage limits and next step
+
+This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
+
+Select an exact case, edition, population, jurisdiction or product version, inspect sources and refine the question before using the existing registry idea/depth planning workflow. These BANK IDs are catalog identities, not approved IDEA IDs. Existing Q1-Q42 defaults, production queues and approval gates are unchanged.
