+| BANK-108-037 | Why can on-time-delivery figures differ even when companies describe the same shipment? | Compare promised date, dispatch, arrival, customer acceptance and exclusions; align definitions before evaluating performance. |
+| BANK-108-038 | How can a supply-chain documentary show a real network without exposing commercial or personal data? | Use authorized records, aggregated routes, consent and clearly labeled illustrative diagrams; distinguish permitted access from independent verification. |
+| BANK-108-039 | What does a disruption postmortem need before calling one event the root cause? | Trace chronology, preexisting constraints, alternatives and evidence; separate triggering events from deeper dependencies and uncertain counterfactuals. |
