+#### BANK-111-001 — Mixed-use neighborhoods
+
+**Video question:** Mixed-use neighborhoods: how do the rules and institutions work in a named jurisdiction?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Cities & Urbanism; branch: Urban form. Address Mixed-use neighborhoods through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Map the responsible institutions, applicable date and jurisdiction for Mixed-use neighborhoods.
+- Trace a documented case or service journey from entry conditions to outcome, distinguishing rules from actual implementation.
+- Compare access, costs, incentives and accountability for different affected groups.
+- Check amendments, exceptions and competing interpretations; identify where qualified local guidance is required.
