+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Social practices
+
+**Research standard:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-149-001 — Hospitality rituals across named communities
+
+**Video question:** Hospitality rituals across named communities: how do participants describe the practice and its differences?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Global Cultures; branch: Social practices. Address Hospitality rituals across named communities through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Choose a specific community and identify who participates in Hospitality rituals across named communities and who may be excluded.
+- Document the actual routines, resources and relationships involved through more than one perspective.
+- Compare change across generations, locations or life circumstances without assuming uniformity.
+- Return to participants for context and consent checks; distinguish their views from the narrator's interpretation.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
