+
+## Detailed subject categories and video questions
+
+### 01. Foundations and vocabulary
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Research direction:** Inspect a named primary-text edition, passage locator, translator and commentary; compare attributions and keep spiritual or symbolic claims in their source context.
+
+**Source leads:** IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite corpus (entry point listed in the batch guide); the named work in a traceable edition; authorized public teaching materials for the tradition concerned. Leads require topic-specific inspection; no entry has verified episode sources yet.
+
+| ID | Specific YouTube episode question | Detailed subtopics and coverage boundary | Suggested registered angle |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| BANK-278-001 | Meditation, relaxation, and concentration: where do their aims differ? | Compare definitions, attention tasks, and intended outcomes without treating the terms as interchangeable. | `beginner_explainers` |
+| BANK-278-002 | What does dhyana mean in Yoga Sutra chapter 3? | Read dharana, dhyana, and samadhi together; compare translations of the same passage. | `beginner_explainers` |
+| BANK-278-003 | What counts as an object of meditation? | Compare breath sensation, a mantra, a visual form, and open awareness as differently defined objects. | `beginner_explainers` |
+| BANK-278-004 | Can meditation include thoughts rather than eliminate them? | Compare instructions on noticing, returning, and nonattachment in two documented methods. | `beginner_explainers` |
+| BANK-278-005 | State versus trait: what does a meditation study measure? | Separate experiences during a session from changes measured outside practice. | `beginner_explainers` |
+| BANK-278-006 | Spiritual liberation and stress reduction: how do meditation goals differ? | Compare an attributed traditional goal with the outcomes of a named secular program. | `beginner_explainers` |
+
