+#### BANK-281-001 — Dosha concepts in classical texts
+
+**Video question:** Dosha concepts in classical texts: how do named sources and interpreters explain it?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Ayurveda; branch: Ayurvedic frameworks. Address Dosha concepts in classical texts through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Identify the source passages, images or authorized descriptions that define Dosha concepts in classical texts.
+- Explain key terms within their own literary, philosophical or devotional setting.
+- Compare a second attributed interpretation without merging distinct traditions or ranking spiritual truth.
+- Document what is uncertain, restricted, disputed or lost in translation; choose visuals that do not invent sacred attributes.
