+#### BANK-289-001 — Mesopotamian temple economies
+
+**Video question:** Mesopotamian temple economies: what do contemporary records establish, and what remains uncertain?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Ancient Religions; branch: Ancient systems. Address Mesopotamian temple economies through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Locate Mesopotamian temple economies in a bounded time and place; build a chronology from identified records.
+- Compare at least two independent witnesses or explain why only one survives.
+- Analyze institutions, material conditions and overlooked participants rather than attributing everything to a single figure.
+- Separate documented conclusions, interpretive debates and gaps that a reconstruction cannot resolve.
+
