+
+- Define Action potentials precisely and identify the scale, system or population being studied.
+- Explain the proposed mechanism with an observable example; distinguish model from direct observation.
+- Inspect how the key quantity is measured and which controls or comparison conditions matter.
+- Discuss uncertainty, alternative explanations and a result that would challenge the account.
