+# 372 Storytelling: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a Storytelling YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-372-01: Narrative tools | media | 3 |
+| CATALOG-372-02: Story forms | media | 3 |
+| CATALOG-372-03: Audience | science | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Narrative tools
+
+**Research standard:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-372-001 — Promise and payoff
+
+**Video question:** Promise and payoff: which creative choices change what the audience understands?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Storytelling; branch: Narrative tools. Address Promise and payoff through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Identify the audience, format and communication problem for Promise and payoff.
+- Annotate a specific scene, design or draft to show how the creative choice works.
+- Compare a revised version and explain what information, feeling or interpretation changes.
+- Check accessibility, rights, consent and possible misreadings before treating the example as a reusable method.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
