+# 374 Science Fiction: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a Science Fiction YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-374-01: Science-fiction premises | fiction | 3 |
+| CATALOG-374-02: World logic | scenario | 3 |
+| CATALOG-374-03: Themes | fiction | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Science-fiction premises
+
+**Research standard:** Create original fiction with explicit world rules, character goals and causal continuity. Label invented events and separate inspiration from claims about actual cultures or living people.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original story notes and world rules; permission-cleared reference material; reader feedback and a continuity audit. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-374-001 — Generation-ship resource politics
+
+**Video question:** How could a story about Generation-ship resource politics develop conflict, consequences and a satisfying resolution?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Science Fiction; branch: Science-fiction premises. Address Generation-ship resource politics through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Define the protagonist's goal and the central conflict in Generation-ship resource politics.
+- Build three causally connected turning points with visible costs and character choices.
+- Plant a detail that earns the ending; test whether a reader can follow the world's rules.
+- Review cultural attribution, consent and sensitive portrayals; label the episode as original fiction.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
