+**Video question:** Categorizing by use frequency: how does it work, and where do its design assumptions fail?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Organization; branch: Practical organization. Address Categorizing by use frequency through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Map the components and operating conditions behind Categorizing by use frequency.
+- Trace a worked example using a diagram, calculation or observed system; state all numerical assumptions.
+- Compare an alternative design against the same requirements; include cost, reliability and accessibility where relevant.
+- Examine a failure mode, measurement error or edge case and show what evidence would change the explanation.
