+# 443 General Knowledge: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a General Knowledge YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-443-01: Scientific literacy | science | 3 |
+| CATALOG-443-02: Civic knowledge | civic | 3 |
+| CATALOG-443-03: Knowledge methods | synthesis | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Scientific literacy
+
+**Research standard:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-443-001 — Units and dimensional reasoning
+
+**Video question:** Units and dimensional reasoning: what mechanisms and measurements support the explanation?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: General Knowledge; branch: Scientific literacy. Address Units and dimensional reasoning through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Define Units and dimensional reasoning precisely and identify the scale, system or population being studied.
+- Explain the proposed mechanism with an observable example; distinguish model from direct observation.
+- Inspect how the key quantity is measured and which controls or comparison conditions matter.
+- Discuss uncertainty, alternative explanations and a result that would challenge the account.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
