+# 451 Literature: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a Literature YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-451-01: Literary forms | history | 3 |
+| CATALOG-451-02: Interpretation | media | 3 |
+| CATALOG-451-03: Textual context | history | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Literary forms
+
+**Research standard:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-451-001 — Epic conventions
+
+**Video question:** Epic conventions: what do contemporary records establish, and what remains uncertain?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Literature; branch: Literary forms. Address Epic conventions through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Locate Epic conventions in a bounded time and place; build a chronology from identified records.
+- Compare at least two independent witnesses or explain why only one survives.
+- Analyze institutions, material conditions and overlooked participants rather than attributing everything to a single figure.
+- Separate documented conclusions, interpretive debates and gaps that a reconstruction cannot resolve.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
