+**Video question:** Interests versus work tasks: how do participants describe the practice and its differences?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Career Guidance; branch: Career decisions. Address Interests versus work tasks through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Choose a specific community and identify who participates in Interests versus work tasks and who may be excluded.
+- Document the actual routines, resources and relationships involved through more than one perspective.
+- Compare change across generations, locations or life circumstances without assuming uniformity.
+- Return to participants for context and consent checks; distinguish their views from the narrator's interpretation.
