+# 492 Ultimate Future of Humanity: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a Ultimate Future of Humanity YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-492-01: Long-term survival | scenario | 3 |
+| CATALOG-492-02: Civilizational continuity | scenario | 3 |
+| CATALOG-492-03: Reasoning | synthesis | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Long-term survival
+
+**Research standard:** Declare a conditional scenario, not a prediction. Anchor present-day capabilities in evidence, make physical and institutional assumptions explicit, and trace second-order consequences and failure conditions.
+
+**Source types to locate:** current original research on the enabling technologies; physical and economic constraints with explicit inputs; published scenario methods and relevant legal frameworks. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-492-001 — Planetary impact defenses
+
+**Video question:** Planetary impact defenses: what follows if the stated assumptions hold?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Ultimate Future of Humanity; branch: Long-term survival. Address Planetary impact defenses through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- List the assumptions that make Planetary impact defenses possible and distinguish demonstrated capability from speculation.
+- Build a resource, energy, time or governance budget appropriate to the scenario.
+- Follow consequences for daily life, institutions and unequal access rather than only depicting impressive technology.
+- Change a major assumption and show how the scenario branches; identify observable evidence that would alter confidence.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
