+# 496 Scam Awareness: Subject Coverage and Episode Proposals
+
+Updated: 2026-10-22 · **Initial subject map; proposed, not researched**
+
+**3 subject categories · 9 topic proposals.**
+
+A starting subject map for a Scam Awareness YouTube channel. Categories organize concrete subtopics; each entry supplies an episode question, a research outline and a boundary for case selection. Counts follow the authored coverage, with no imposed topic maximum.
+
+[All-niche index](../ALL_NICHE_TOPIC_BANKS.md) · [Editable JSON](./IN_DEPTH_TOPIC_BANK.json) · [Expansion method](../ALL_NICHE_EXPANSION_GUIDE.md)
+
+This is a first coverage pass with concrete subject headings and research briefs. It has less editorial depth than the 120-question Meditation, Pranayama and Yoga pilots. It is not exhaustive, and has no fixed topic limit. The suggested research questions and outlines use domain-specific editorial patterns; they are proposals to refine against actual sources, not evidence that the research has been done.
+
+The IDs refer to catalog entries, not episodes produced. Angles are deliberately unassigned until the actual niche angle scope and selected case are reviewed. No topic is ready_for_project or verified. The research outline is not a follow-along lesson, treatment plan, legal instruction, investment recommendation or hazardous procedure.
+
+## Subject map
+
+| Category | Research mode | Topic proposals |
+|---|---|---:|
+| CATALOG-496-01: Scam mechanisms | civic | 3 |
+| CATALOG-496-02: Digital channels | digital | 3 |
+| CATALOG-496-03: Verification | civic | 3 |
+
+## Detailed proposals
+
+### Scam mechanisms
+
+**Research standard:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-496-001 — Urgency and authority impersonation
+
+**Video question:** Urgency and authority impersonation: how do the rules and institutions work in a named jurisdiction?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Scam Awareness; branch: Scam mechanisms. Address Urgency and authority impersonation through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Map the responsible institutions, applicable date and jurisdiction for Urgency and authority impersonation.
+- Trace a documented case or service journey from entry conditions to outcome, distinguishing rules from actual implementation.
+- Compare access, costs, incentives and accountability for different affected groups.
+- Check amendments, exceptions and competing interpretations; identify where qualified local guidance is required.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
