+#### BANK-499-001 — Deductibles and exclusions
+
+**Video question:** Deductibles and exclusions: which assumptions change the costs, risks and outcomes?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Insurance Education; branch: Insurance mechanics. Address Deductibles and exclusions through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Specify the institution, product, market or household scenario behind Deductibles and exclusions, with date and jurisdiction.
+- Work through a numerical example with explicit fees, cash flows and assumptions; label invented figures as illustrative.
+- Stress-test a different price, income, rate or time horizon and identify who bears the risk.
+- Compare official terms with common promotional claims and list the unresolved information a decision would require.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
