+### Retirement planning
+
+**Research standard:** Use current official terms, filings or macroeconomic data; state jurisdiction, date, fees, taxes, risk, units and assumptions. Use transparent illustrative calculations rather than personal recommendations or return promises.
+
+**Source types to locate:** regulator or official statistical publications; actual contracts, fee schedules and audited filings; original economic studies and disclosed calculation inputs. These source types are not topic-specific sources already inspected.
+
+#### BANK-500-001 — Longevity risk
+
+**Video question:** Longevity risk: which assumptions change the costs, risks and outcomes?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Retirement Education; branch: Retirement planning. Address Longevity risk through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Specify the institution, product, market or household scenario behind Longevity risk, with date and jurisdiction.
+- Work through a numerical example with explicit fees, cash flows and assumptions; label invented figures as illustrative.
+- Stress-test a different price, income, rate or time horizon and identify who bears the risk.
+- Compare official terms with common promotional claims and list the unresolved information a decision would require.
+
+**Next action:** Select and inspect a concrete case and traceable sources; record unresolved questions before choosing a registered angle and promoting an episode idea.
