+#### BANK-504-001 — Antenatal care access
+
+**Video question:** Antenatal care access: what does current evidence establish for a defined population?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Maternal & Child Health; branch: Maternal health. Address Antenatal care access through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Define Antenatal care access, the population and the outcome; distinguish normal variation, symptoms, screening and diagnosis where applicable.
+- Explain the relevant mechanism without turning a plausible mechanism into proof of a clinical effect.
+- Compare actual study designs, outcomes and follow-up; inspect harms, missing data and generalizability.
+- State the evidence limits and the boundary between public education and an individual's clinical assessment.
+
