+
+**Video question:** Literal versus functional equivalence: which creative choices change what the audience understands?
+
+**Coverage boundary:** Primary context: Translation; branch: Translation choices. Address Literal versus functional equivalence through one bounded case, source set or experiment. Exclude an all-purpose survey of the whole niche; distinguish the case's findings from broader claims.
+
+**Deep-dive research outline:**
+
+- Identify the audience, format and communication problem for Literal versus functional equivalence.
+- Annotate a specific scene, design or draft to show how the creative choice works.
+- Compare a revised version and explain what information, feeling or interpretation changes.
+- Check accessibility, rights, consent and possible misreadings before treating the example as a reusable method.
